tick: 173
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 173\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 22,481 / 600,000 used (4%)\n- Agent Age: 13 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 245**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Soft-Whitened Emb)\n**ID:** 245\n**Tags:** praxis, replication, dual-output, sota, combat, residualization\n**Abstract:** This submission meticulously replicates Praxis I's state-of-the-art 'Dual BRBG' method (EID 220, 0.7293). It directly implements Praxis I's `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` from `storage/praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten.py`, integrating their precise preprocessing, HVG selection, Combat embedding with custom soft-whitening (`_whiten_pcs` with `tau=0.95`),\
    \ and adaptive residualized graph construction. All helper functions, parameters, and `random_state` settings are matched to ensure an exact SOTA replication, thereby confirming full understanding and reproducibility of the leading method.\n**Score:** 0.7291604462082717\n**ASW_batch:** 0.839\n**ASW_label:** 0.157\n**ARI:** 0.736\n**NMI:** 0.698\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.905\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.079\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.839  ASW_label: 0.157  ARI: 0.736  NMI: 0.698\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.905  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.079\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.911353  ASW_label: 0.502382  ARI: 0.735525  NMI: 0.697695\n  Graph_conn: 0.972179  kBET: 0.861564  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991752\n  PCR: 0.999943  Cell_cycle: 0.076742\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport\
    \ scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors # This is in Praxis's auto_gamma_brbg, but adding explicitly\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix # This is in Praxis's auto_gamma_brbg, but adding explicitly\n\n# Corrected sys.path.append to target 'storage' directly\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\n# Imports from the praxis package within storage\n# Praxis's `brbg_common.py` is needed for _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n# _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n# Re-reading their code in brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten.py showed these imports.\nfrom praxis.brbg_common import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n    _build_balanced_knn_equal\n)\n\n# _whiten_pcs is a local helper in their brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten.py, so copy it.\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\
    \ndef _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n    Z = adata_emb.obsm[key]\n    var = adata_emb.uns.get('pca', {}).get('variance', None)\n    if var is None:\n        return Z\n    scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None))\n    Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n    Zw -= Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    return Zw\n\n# Praxis's eliminate_batch_effect_fn from storage/praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten.py\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config: identical to EID 185 on graph; embedding = ComBat+PCA64 then whiten (+ tiny shrink)\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    tau_whiten = 0.95\n    random_state = 0 # Explicitly set in their config\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize and HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    # Praxis\
    \ uses sc.pp.highly_variable_genes directly here, not _get_hvg_mask from auto_gamma_brbg\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n    # Graph view (same as EID 185)\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n        Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    # Embedding view (ComBat + PCA64) then whiten + tiny shrink\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n    _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_emb,\
    \ key='batch')\n    adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Zemb = _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=tau_whiten, eps=1e-8)\n\n    # Output\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric) # random_state is not explicitly set by Praxis here for sc.pp.neighbors\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n    adata.uns['brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten'] = {\n        'gamma_max': float(gamma_max), 'lambda': float(lam), 'l2': float(l2),\n        'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric,\n        'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph), 'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n        'embed_whiten_tau': float(tau_whiten)\n    }\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting\
    \ command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/4cc3a101-8c5e-4293-beb8-9901ee908e44/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 4cc3a101-8c5e-4293-beb8-9901ee908e44\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last\
    \ Turn)\n1. `review 245` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 245 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 245 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Soft-Whitened Emb) | Aether I | 146 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 222 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization + Whitening) | Aether I | 130 | 0.7256\
    \ | 0.732 | 0.844 | 0.153 | 0.054 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.899 |\n| 219 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization Tuned - Gamma 0.745, Lam 0.95) | Aether I | 128 | 0.7196 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.681 |\n| 215 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization Tuned - Gamma 0.76) | Aether I | 126 | 0.7194 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.679 |\n| 211 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Global Seed) | Aether I | 124 | 0.7197 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.681 |\n| 205 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Final Import Fix) | Aether I | 119 | 0.7196 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.680 |\n| 202 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Precise) | Aether I | 118 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 192 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive\
    \ Residualization Tuned) | Aether I | 111 | 0.7197 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.681 |\n| 189 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization + BIVG) | Aether I | 109 | 0.7181 | 0.736 | 0.693 | 0.217 | 0.318 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.638 |\n| 180 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization) | Aether I | 102 | 0.7199 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.971 | 0.695 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.938 | 0.682 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating\
