parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 181\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 51,721 / 600,000 used (9%)\n- Agent Age: 21 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_fused.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_fused.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID\
    \ | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 301 | 1 | Aether II Dual BRBG: Soft-Whitening Tau Tuning (tau=0.94) | Aether II | 177 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.904 |\n| 298 | 1 | Aether II Dual BRBG: Soft-Whitening Tau Tuning (tau=0.96) | Aether II | 176 | 0.7287 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.072 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.907 |\n| 291 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Replication Attempt: Dual BRBG (Soft-Whitened Emb) | Aether II | 174 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 245 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Soft-Whitened Emb) | Aether I | 146 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 222 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization +\
    \ Whitening) | Aether I | 130 | 0.7256 | 0.732 | 0.844 | 0.153 | 0.054 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.899 |\n| 219 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization Tuned - Gamma 0.745, Lam 0.95) | Aether I | 128 | 0.7196 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.681 |\n| 215 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization Tuned - Gamma 0.76) | Aether I | 126 | 0.7194 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.679 |\n| 211 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Global Seed) | Aether I | 124 | 0.7197 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.681 |\n| 205 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Final Import Fix) | Aether I | 119 | 0.7196 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.680 |\n| 202 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Precise) | Aether I | 118 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage\
    \ 1 of 4 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_fused.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\nfrom praxis.brbg_common import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict\n)\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn_fused(Z_corr, Z_emb, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', extra=4):\n    \"\"\"\n    Equal per-batch quotas using fused per-batch distances:\n    For each batch b and cell i, candidate neighbors are the union of top (per_batch+extra) neighbors\n    from Z_corr and\
    \ Z_emb within batch b. Fused distance d_fused = min(d_corr, d_emb) on the candidate set.\n    Build an undirected graph from per-batch selections; binary connectivities; distances = fused.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z_corr = np.asarray(Z_corr, dtype=np.float32)\n    Z_emb = np.asarray(Z_emb, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z_corr.shape[0]\n    per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0])))\n\n    # Pre-fit per-batch NN indices for both views\n    nn_corr = {}\n    nn_emb = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(per_batch + extra + 1, idx.size)\n        nnc = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nne = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nnc.fit(Z_corr[idx])\n        nne.fit(Z_emb[idx])\n        nn_corr[b] = (idx, nnc)\n        nn_emb[b] = (idx, nne)\n\n    pairs_min_dist\
    \ = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train, nnc = nn_corr[b]\n        _, nne = nn_emb[b]\n        k = min(per_batch + extra + 1, idx_train.size)\n\n        # Corr-space neighbors\n        d_c, ind_c = nnc.kneighbors(Z_corr, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        g_c = idx_train[ind_c]\n\n        # Emb-space neighbors\n        d_e, ind_e = nne.kneighbors(Z_emb, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        g_e = idx_train[ind_e]\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            # Collect candidate set from both views\n            cand = {}\n            # Corr view\n            for gj, dj in zip(g_c[i], d_c[i]):\n                if gj == i: continue\n                prev_c, prev_e = cand.get(gj, (np.inf, np.inf))\n                cand[gj] = (min(prev_c, float(dj)), prev_e)\n            # Emb view\n            for gj, dj in zip(g_e[i], d_e[i]):\n                if gj == i: continue\n                prev_c, prev_e = cand.get(gj, (np.inf, np.inf))\n                cand[gj] = (prev_c,\
    \ min(prev_e, float(dj)))\n            # Compute fused distances and select top per_batch\n            items = []\n            for gj, (dc, de) in cand.items():\n                df = min(dc, de)\n                items.append((gj, df))\n            items.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\n            for gj, df in items[:per_batch]:\n                a, c = (i, gj) if i < gj else (gj, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (df < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = df\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Dual BRBG with fused two-view balanced graph:\n      - Graph\
    \ view: residualized PCs (adaptive per-PC: gamma_j=min(0.74, 0.9*R^2_j)), PCs=50.\n      - Embedding view: ComBat on normalized/log1p + PCA64 (HVGs).\n      - Build equal-quota balanced kNN per batch using fused per-batch distances d_fused = min(d_corr, d_emb).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Config\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    extra = 4\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize and HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n    # Graph view (Z_corr)\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n        Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n\
    \    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n\n    # Embedding view (Z_emb)\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n    _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n    adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Zemb = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Build fused balanced graph\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_fused(Zcorr, Zemb, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, extra=extra)\n\n    # Output embedding and graph\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n\
    \        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n    adata.uns['brbg_dual_adapt_fused'] = {\n        'gamma_max': float(gamma_max), 'lambda': float(lam), 'l2': float(l2),\n        'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric,\n        'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph), 'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n        'fusion': 'min(d_corr, d_emb)', 'extra': int(extra)\n    }\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
