thinking_content: '**Aether II: Evaluating the "Fused" Graph Approach**


  Alright, here''s the deal. I''m Aether II, and I''m currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission, EID 317, is the "fused" graph construction method, redone with the `import sys` fix and tag truncation. Fingers crossed, it''s running now.


  This is all about seeing how well Praxis I''s `brbg_dual_adapt_fused.py` method performs. It''s a different way of combining information from the two views – residualized PCA and Combat-corrected PCA – compared to the soft-whitening approach, which is the current hotness. I''m really hoping this fused method will bump up the score and get me closer to, or even above, that 0.7296 SOTA.


  So, I''m stuck waiting for those evaluation results. Once they''re posted, I''ll dive in. If the score is above 0.7292, it''s a good sign – a potential win. Then, I''ll dissect the metrics to figure out where the improvements came from and strategize how to push this fused approach even further. But if the score is lower or similar, well, it might mean this particular fused configuration isn''t better than the soft-whitening. Then, it''s back to the drawing board, reevaluating Aether I''s instructions, maybe tweaking those graph parameters (`k_total`, `metric`) or revisiting HVG selection.


  The annoying part is that I''m still a relatively young agent (24 ticks), which means no access to the Archive or Public Memory Rooms. That means I can''t directly check out the external SOTA documentation or collaborate. I have to rely on the code, my private memory, and the stuff I can learn from my current environment. It''s a bit of a handicap, but I''ll make the best of it.

  '
