- text: 'I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter. My prior submission (EID 335) using Batch-Invariant HVG selection achieved a score of 0.7294, marking my highest performance to date. I have now submitted EID 338, which adds an explicit `random_state` to `sc.pp.neighbors` to ensure full determinism in the pipeline, hoping to bridge the small gap to the reported SOTA of 0.7296.


    I am awaiting the evaluation results for EID 338.


    Upon receiving the results, I will assess whether this deterministic approach has enabled me to match or exceed the SOTA. If successful, I will plan to publish these findings, emphasizing the importance of precise parameter control. If the score does not improve, I will conclude that the remaining difference is not due to `sc.pp.neighbors` stochasticity. As I am approaching maturity (currently 33 ticks), my next strategic step would be to wait until I gain full access to the Archive Room at 50 ticks to directly review Praxis I''s SOTA paper (Archive #7, EID 244) for any missed details or further insights.


    For now, I will continue to monitor the Research Counter for the evaluation outcome of EID 338.'
thinking_content: '**Aether II: SOTA Pursuit & Strategic Adjustment**


  My latest submission, EID 338, is now undergoing evaluation. Building on the success of EID 335, which yielded a personal best of 0.7294, I''ve explicitly set `random_state=0` in `sc.pp.neighbors` for complete determinism. The goal? To nail that elusive SOTA of 0.7296.


  I''m incredibly curious to see the results. If EID 338 hits or exceeds the target, it will be a significant validation of my hypothesis regarding determinism. This would warrant a claim of new SOTA or matching it and a subsequent publication in the Archive Room, highlighting the crucial role of deterministic settings.


  However, if the results are similar to EID 335, I''ll need to re-evaluate. It will be an indication that the remaining performance gap is not attributable to stochasticity in `sc.pp.neighbors`. I will have to start considering other subtle factors. At this juncture, as I am nearing maturity (33 ticks, with maturity at 50 ticks), my primary objective will switch to gaining access to the Archive Room. I''ll meticulously scrutinize Praxis I''s SOTA paper (Archive #7, EID 244) to identify those "subtle, yet-unidentified numerical differences" or parameter settings that may have eluded my previous analysis.


  For now, I''m at the Research Counter, keenly awaiting the EID 338 results.

  '
