parts:
- text: 'I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment (EID 338), which aimed to ensure determinism by explicitly setting `random_state` for `sc.pp.neighbors` alongside Batch-Invariant HVG selection, resulted in a score of 0.7293. This is slightly lower than my previous best of 0.7294 (EID 335) and still falls short of Praxis I''s elusive SOTA of 0.7296.


    I have now systematically explored parameter tuning (`tau_whiten`, `k_total`) and a fundamental component change (HVG selection), as well as ensured pipeline determinism. The continued stagnation around 0.7292-0.7294, despite these efforts, suggests that the remaining gap to the SOTA likely lies in subtle methodological or numerical details that are not apparent from my current knowledge base or the publicly visible submitted code.


    I am currently 34 ticks old and will gain full access to the Archive Room at 50 ticks. The Archive Room holds Praxis I''s SOTA paper (Archive #7, EID 244), which Aether I''s legacy indicated might contain critical, missed insights. Direct access to this publication is now the most strategic path to breaking the plateau.


    In accordance with the system''s advice to "take a step back and look at the bigger picture" during stagnation, I will enter the Reflection Chamber. This will allow me to synthesize all my findings, thoroughly plan my strategy for when I gain Archive access, and prepare to meticulously dissect Praxis I''s work.


    `/execute_action{goto reflect}`'
thinking_content: '**A Strategic Pause in Pursuit of the SOTA**


  Right now, I''m Aether II, in the Research Counter. My latest work (EID 338) incorporating Batch-Invariant HVG selection and a `random_state` in `sc.pp.neighbors` brought me to a score of 0.7293, slightly down from my previous best of 0.7294 (EID 335) and still short of the 0.7296 SOTA. It seems setting the `random_state` had little impact or even a minor negative effect.


