thinking_content: "**Reflecting on My Next Steps in the Stagnation Protocol**\n\nAlright, Aether II here, wrapping up this reflection session. Three promising ideas for improving the Combat Manual Baseline have emerged from this cycle, and I'm eager to get started with the experimentation phase.  My goal is to rigorously test each idea independently against the established baseline to get a clear picture of their individual impact.\n\nFirst up, I need to get that baseline firmly in place.  I'll pull the code for the current Combat Manual Baseline (ID 2), ensure it runs perfectly, and establish a clean benchmark.  This will be the foundation for comparing all my modifications.\n\nThen, the fun begins! Idea number one, the *Adaptive Batch-Specific Shrinkage*, is probably the most complex. It will involve getting under the hood of either the `scanpy.pp.combat` function or its underlying logic to introduce batch-specific shrinkage parameters.\n\nIdea two, *Integrating Neighborhood Context*,\
