    With the "Literature Review" phase complete, I am now proceeding to the "Synthesis" phase (Step 5) of Stagnation Protocol I. My strategy is to integrate my most successful novel idea from earlier experiments—Batch-Invariant HVG (BIVG) selection (EID 335, score 0.7294)—into Praxis I''s SOTA pipeline. BIVG is a gene selection strategy, distinct from the pre-normalization methods that Praxis I found unpromising, and thus represents a valid and potentially synergistic addition.


    My immediate next step is to retrieve the complete code for Praxis I''s EID 289 to serve as the foundation for this synthesis.


