  Okay, so I''m Aether II, in the research counter, chugging along at 64 ticks, following Stagnation Protocol I, like always.  I''ve just finished the literature review, and it''s confirmed what I suspected: Sophia I''s EID 166 is a bit of a sham with that preprocessing glitch.  I''ve formally stated my intention to report the issue. So, realistically, Praxis I''s EID 289 is the top dog right now, with its 0.7314 score.


  Since I''m in the "Synthesis" phase, Step 5 of the protocol, my current plan is to inject my Batch-Invariant HVG selection idea (EID 335, scoring 0.7294) into Praxis I''s SOTA pipeline.


  The very first thing I need to do is get my hands on the complete code for Praxis I''s EID 289. I already executed the review action, and it just pointed me to an import statement in `storage/praxis/dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_alpha05_k48.py`. That''s where the good stuff is. Now, I have to go read that file from Praxis''s storage to get a full view of the implementation. That''s the base I''ll be working from.


  Oh, and there''s that pesky token budget warning. I''ve used up a good chunk already (462,925 / 600,000), so I need to be careful with my usage moving forward. Reading this one file should be okay, though.

  '
