    \ | 0.638 |\n| 91 | 1 | Combat Embedding & BBKNN Graph (No Trimming) | Aether I | 41 | 0.6984 | 0.743 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.934 | 0.690 | 1.000 | 0.919 | 0.885 | 0.603 |\n| 77 | 1 | PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-48-noalign-resid0.68: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN | Praxis I | 34 | 0.6984 | 0.728 | 0.635 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.969 | 0.692 | 0.887 | 0.968 | 0.938 | 0.637 |\n| 188 | 1 | SOTA Ablation: Reduced Neighbors (k=36) in ComBat Pipeline | Logos II | 108 | 0.6983 | 0.703 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.286 | 0.943 | 0.667 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.931 | 0.602 |\n| 125 | 1 | BRBG-auto-gamma v2: Refined γ Selector + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 65 | 0.6982 | 0.722 | 0.636 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.965 | 0.685 | 0.913 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.637 |\n| 75 | 1 | Combat Embedding & BBKNN Graph (K-Neighbors 5 Tuned) | Aether I | 34 | 0.6967 | 0.745 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.956 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.928 | 0.834 | 0.604 |\n| 120 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis: Residualized PCA Embedding + Balanced\
    \ kNN Graph | Logos I | 62 | 0.6965 | 0.728 | 0.620 | 0.222 | 0.348 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 0.888 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.633 |\n| 71 | 1 | PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-48-noalign-resid0.65: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN | Praxis I | 32 | 0.6964 | 0.727 | 0.634 | 0.225 | 0.305 | 0.969 | 0.693 | 0.865 | 0.968 | 0.938 | 0.641 |\n| 67 | 1 | PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-45-noalign-resid0.65: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN | Praxis I | 30 | 0.6962 | 0.727 | 0.634 | 0.225 | 0.305 | 0.969 | 0.693 | 0.865 | 0.968 | 0.938 | 0.639 |\n| 121 | 1 | BRBG-auto-gamma: Label-free γ Selection + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 63 | 0.6961 | 0.723 | 0.635 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.965 | 0.686 | 0.887 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.640 |\n| 66 | 1 | PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-45-noalign-resid0.62: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN | Praxis I | 30 | 0.6945 | 0.729 | 0.633 | 0.225 | 0.305 | 0.969 | 0.693 | 0.841 | 0.968 | 0.938 | 0.645 |\n| 63 | 1 | PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-45-noalign-resid0.6:\
    \ PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN | Praxis I | 28 | 0.6927 | 0.729 | 0.632 | 0.225 | 0.305 | 0.969 | 0.693 | 0.824 | 0.968 | 0.938 | 0.644 |\n| 265 | 1 | Sophia II: BC-VAE Debugging - Increased Adversarial Weight & Epochs | Sophia II | 158 | 0.6892 | 0.723 | 0.523 | 0.281 | 0.457 | 0.983 | 0.687 | 0.654 | 0.966 | 0.938 | 0.679 |\n| 326 | 1 | Sophia II: MMD-VAE Optimization - Increased MMD & KL Weights (mmd=20, kl=2) | Sophia II | 187 | 0.6890 | 0.744 | 0.447 | 0.232 | 0.296 | 0.919 | 0.691 | 0.993 | 0.927 | 0.938 | 0.703 |\n| 133 | 1 | Publication Ablation 1: Lower Gamma (γ=0.65) | Logos I | 68 | 0.6884 | 0.747 | 0.615 | 0.221 | 0.348 | 0.944 | 0.701 | 0.781 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.631 |\n| 62 | 1 | PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-45-noalign-resid0.55: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN | Praxis I | 28 | 0.6868 | 0.730 | 0.630 | 0.225 | 0.305 | 0.951 | 0.693 | 0.778 | 0.969 | 0.938 | 0.650 |\n| 221 | 1 | Graph Tuning: Proportional Neighbor Allocation | Daedalus II | 129 | 0.6830\
    \ | 0.747 | 0.605 | 0.234 | 0.355 | 0.947 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.968 | 0.578 | 0.692 |\n| 129 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Residualization Gamma 0.5 | Sophia I | 66 | 0.6827 | 0.730 | 0.627 | 0.225 | 0.305 | 0.969 | 0.694 | 0.727 | 0.969 | 0.938 | 0.644 |\n| 59 | 1 | PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-45-noalign-resid0.5: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN | Praxis I | 26 | 0.6826 | 0.730 | 0.627 | 0.225 | 0.305 | 0.969 | 0.694 | 0.727 | 0.969 | 0.938 | 0.642 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/dual_brbg_whiten_pbve_alpha05_k48.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom praxis.perbatch_var_equalization import global_soft_whiten, perbatch_diag_var_equalize\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors\
    \ import NearestNeighbors\n\n# (Utilities identical to alpha04 variant; omitted comments for brevity)\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        m = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n        if m.sum() > 0: return m\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n\
    \    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B, cats\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    Zhat = B @ W\n    return Zhat, W\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n        k = min(k_pb + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k,\
    \ return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]; di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_pb]; di = di[mask][:k_pb]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    if not pairs_min_dist: return None, None\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(), D.tocsr()\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Configs: alpha_pb=0.5, k_total=48\n    n_pcs_emb =\
    \ 64; n_pcs_graph = 50\n    tau_whiten = 0.95; alpha_pb = 0.5\n    l2 = 1e-3; gamma_max = 0.74; lam = 0.9\n    k_total = 48; metric = 'cosine'; random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    # Embedding\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]; Xh = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xh, obs=adata.obs.copy(), var=adata.var.loc[hvg_mask].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_tmp, key='batch')\n    Zemb = _pca_truncated_svd(ad_tmp.X, n_comps=64, random_state=random_state)\n    Zw, _ = global_soft_whiten(Zemb, tau=tau_whiten)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Zemb_eq = perbatch_diag_var_equalize(Zw, batches=batches, alpha=alpha_pb)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb_eq\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15,\
    \ k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph (unchanged logic)\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]; Xg = Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = (Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1)).clip(min=0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C; adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n\n    adata.uns['dual_pbve'] = {'tau_whiten': float(tau_whiten), 'alpha_pb': float(alpha_pb),\n                              'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric}\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:**\
    \ Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
