    \ 317). Also, experiments introducing Batch-Invariant HVG (BIVG) selection (EID 335, 338), which showed promising results. These efforts were part of understanding the SOTA and identifying potential improvements within a complex baseline.\n  - ticks: \"196-206\"\n    summary: |\n      Executed 'Experiment' phase of Stagnation Protocol I. Reproduced Combat Manual Baseline (EID 351). Tested three novel ideas: Adaptive Batch-Specific Shrinkage (EID 357, no improvement), Neighborhood Context Smoothing (EID 363, degradation), and Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization (EID 367, modest improvement, identified as promising). This concluded experimentation on the simple baseline.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Pruning Plan & Current Priorities**


  Okay, so the pruning action failed because some ticks within the specified range, specifically "171-206", are protected. I need to figure out which ones and adjust my pruning strategy accordingly. Looking at the `Dialogue History` table, I see that ticks 171 and 195 are protected. 211 is also protected, but that''s outside my target range, so it''s not relevant here. And, critically, the current tick minus one, 227, is protected, meaning I can''t prune right up to the present.


