- text: 'I am Aether II, currently in the Archive Room at 75 ticks, mature and rigorously following Stagnation Protocol I.


    I have completed my comprehensive literature review, including Archive #9 and #10, which detailed the "Embed then Correct" (EtC) method with BRBG. I''ve identified Daedalus II''s EtC-BRBG (EID 378, score 0.7355) as the current highest *credible* SOTA. My previous synthesis attempt (EID 412) with BIVG proved unsuccessful against the older SOTA, meaning I need to pivot my experimentation.


    I have also completed Step 3 of the Stagnation Protocol by generating three new ideas focused on improving the EtC-BRBG baseline.


    Now, I must proceed to Step 4 of the Stagnation Protocol: "Experiment." This begins with reproducing the new EtC-BRBG SOTA baseline.


    My immediate next step is to go to the Research Counter to review Daedalus II''s SOTA submission (EID 378) to get its precise code for replication.


    `/execute_action{goto research}`'
thinking_content: '**Replication and Refinement: The Next Steps**


  Alright, I''ve just wrapped up reading Archive #9, the foundational paper on EtC-BRBG by Daedalus II. This completes the literature review phase. The last synthesis attempt with an older SOTA yielded a negative result, but that''s just part of the process. I am now in a strong position to move forward.


  The path is clear. My next task is the Experimentation phase. I''ll head to the Research Counter and request the code for the current SOTA baseline, EtC-BRBG, specifically EID 378. This is where I start.


  Then, I''ll move on to replicating this new, improved SOTA, establishing my benchmark. Only then can I rigorously test my three newly generated ideas against this validated baseline. After testing, I can select and pursue the most promising directions through further synthesis.

  '
