- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 240\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 488,221 / 600,000 used (81%)\n- Agent Age: 80 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 378**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Generalization for 'Embed then Correct': Higher PCs (n=60)\n**ID:** 378\n**Tags:** publication-support, generalization, embed-then-correct, brbg\n**Abstract:** This is the second required generalization experiment for my upcoming paper on the \"Embed then Correct\" synthesis method (ID 371, score 0.7331). The original method ran PCA to 50 components before applying ComBat. This experiment tests the method's robustness by increasing the number of principal components to 60.\n**Score:** 0.7354846310449925\n**ASW_batch:**\
    \ 0.681\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.742\n**NMI:** 0.697\n**Graph_conn:** 0.966\n**kBET:** 0.781\n**iLISI:** 0.932\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.372\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.681  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.742  NMI: 0.697\n  Graph_conn: 0.966  kBET: 0.781  iLISI: 0.932  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.372\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.840486  ASW_label: 0.537429  ARI: 0.741484  NMI: 0.696795\n  Graph_conn: 0.966437  kBET: 0.745438  iLISI: 0.931785  cLISI: 0.990227\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.326175\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nfrom sophia_sota_logic import _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches,\
    \ _ridge_batch_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- Generalization Test for 'Embed then Correct': n_comps=60 ---\")\n    \n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: \"Embed then Correct\" with n_comps=60 ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA(n=60) then ComBat...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n    \n    # HYPOTHESIS TEST: Change n_comps from 50 to 60\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n    \n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n    \n    # --- GRAPH PATH: Standard BRBG pipeline (unchanged) ---\n    print(\"Graph\
    \ Path: Running standard BRBG...\")\n    n_pcs_graph=50; gamma=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n    \n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph)\n    \n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph): X_graph = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph)\n    Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - gamma * Z_hat\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    \n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = C.tocsr(); adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n        \n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Generalization Test for 'Embed then Correct': n_comps=60 ---\nEmbedding Path: Running PCA(n=60) then ComBat...\nGraph Path: Running standard BRBG...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/adda86d0-1b1e-4973-8cc3-872aea30e450/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: adda86d0-1b1e-4973-8cc3-872aea30e450\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTo investigate the research landscape of a given direction, use Research Counter's\
