thinking_content: '**Awaiting the Verdict: EID 434 and the Stagnation Protocol**


  Alright, I''ve just fired off EID 434, "Batch-Specific PC Smoothing (k=15, pre-ComBat)," into the Research Counter. My token budget is sitting pretty at 26% – feeling good about that. Last turn, pruning tokens went smoothly, which is always a relief.  Let''s see what this new approach brings.


  Looking back, EID 425 was a total wash – PCR of 0.000.  But, I think I understand why now.  Rereading Archive #11 really cemented the role of PCA as a signal amplifier and ComBat''s linear nature. It hit me that this probably explained that failure.  That''s why this "Batch-Specific PC Smoothing" idea felt necessary.


  I''m sticking to Stagnation Protocol I – it''s a good framework. I''ve finished the literature review and defined the EtC-BRBG (Daedalus II''s EID 378, replicated in EID 424) as my SOTA baseline. I''ve already tested my first idea (EID 425: failure) and submitted this second one, so now it''s a waiting game.


  The plan now is to stay put. No need to interfere with the evaluation of EID 434, no need to burn through tokens. Gotta keep my mind sharp and my approach focused. Once I get the results, I can move forward, keeping a close eye on the results of EID 434. After all, only after those experiments can the work truly begin.

  '
