parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 252\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 263,336 / 600,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 92 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aether II EtC-BRBG: Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization (Pre-PCA)' (ID: 439) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5946064918595991\n**ASW_batch:** 0.683\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.459\n**NMI:** 0.663\n**Graph_conn:** 0.881\n**kBET:** 0.682\n**iLISI:** 0.019\n**cLISI:** 0.988\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.353\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.683  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.459  NMI: 0.663\n  Graph_conn: 0.881  kBET: 0.682  iLISI: 0.019  cLISI: 0.988\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle:\
    \ 0.353\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.841345  ASW_label: 0.537302  ARI: 0.459034  NMI: 0.663312\n  Graph_conn: 0.882575  kBET: 0.652686  iLISI: 0.019203  cLISI: 0.996423\n  PCR: 0.999982  Cell_cycle: 0.309779\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 439\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission code in version v3. The code is now running without crashes.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical bugs in the `_batch_specific_quantile_normalize` function:\n\n1. **Variable Name Error (v1)**: The function parameter was named `adata_X` but the code tried to access `adata.var['batch_hvg']` on line 15. This caused a `NameError: name 'adata' is not defined`.\n\n2. **Sparse Matrix Assignment Error (v2)**: After fixing the variable name, the code attempted to assign a sparse matrix back to a slice of another sparse matrix using `normalized_X[batch_mask, hvg_indices] = csr_matrix(...)`. This caused a `ValueError: shape mismatch` because\
    \ scipy's sparse matrix slicing doesn't support direct assignment of sparse matrices.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (Fixed NameError)\nChanged the function signature and call to pass the full `adata` object instead of just `adata.X`:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\ndef _batch_specific_quantile_normalize(adata_X, batch_labels, n_genes_hvg=2000):\n    normalized_X = adata_X.copy()\n    hvg_mask = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values  # NameError: adata not defined\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\ndef _batch_specific_quantile_normalize(adata, batch_labels, n_genes_hvg=2000):\n    normalized_X = adata.X.copy()\n    hvg_mask = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values  # Now adata is available\n```\n\nAnd updated the call site:\n```python\n# Before: adata.X = _batch_specific_quantile_normalize(adata.X, adata.obs['batch'].astype('category'))\n# After:\nadata.X = _batch_specific_quantile_normalize(adata, adata.obs['batch'].astype('category'))\n```\n\n### Version 3 (Fixed Sparse Matrix Assignment)\nInstead of trying\
    \ to assign a sparse matrix back to a sparse matrix slice, the code now:\n\n1. Updates the dense `hvg_data` array directly during the batch normalization loop\n2. Uses proper sparse matrix handling when assigning back to `normalized_X`:\n\n**Before (v2):**\n```python\nnormalized_flat_batch_hvg = np.interp(ranks, ...)\nnormalized_X[batch_mask, hvg_indices] = csr_matrix(normalized_flat_batch_hvg.reshape(original_shape))\n# ValueError: shape mismatch during sparse matrix assignment\n```\n\n**After (v3):**\n```python\nnormalized_flat_batch_hvg = np.interp(ranks, ...)\n# Update the dense array directly\nhvg_data[batch_mask, :] = normalized_flat_batch_hvg.reshape(original_shape)\n\n# After loop, assign back properly handling sparse matrices\nif issparse(normalized_X):\n    normalized_X = normalized_X.tolil()  # Convert to lil for efficient item assignment\n    for i, gene_idx in enumerate(hvg_indices):\n        normalized_X[:, gene_idx] = hvg_data[:, i].reshape(-1, 1)\n    normalized_X = normalized_X.tocsr()\
    \  # Convert back to csr\nelse:\n    normalized_X[:, hvg_indices] = hvg_data\n```\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe fix handles sparse matrices correctly by:\n- Converting to LIL (List of Lists) format for efficient column-wise assignment\n- Iterating through each HVG column and assigning the normalized dense data\n- Converting back to CSR (Compressed Sparse Row) format for efficiency\n\n## Result\nThe code now runs successfully without crashes. The monitor script confirmed that version v3 has been running for 300+ seconds without errors, which indicates the fix is working correctly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, issparse\nimport pandas as pd\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/aether')\nfrom aether_utils import _normalize_log1p_inplace,\
    \ _build_balanced_knn\n\ndef _batch_specific_quantile_normalize(adata, batch_labels, n_genes_hvg=2000):\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs batch-specific quantile normalization on highly variable genes in adata.\n    Each batch's HVG distribution is normalized to the global HVG distribution.\n    \"\"\"\n    normalized_X = adata.X.copy()\n\n    # Ensure batch_labels is categorical and access categories correctly\n    if not isinstance(batch_labels.dtype, pd.CategoricalDtype):\n        batch_labels = batch_labels.astype('category')\n    batches = batch_labels.cat.categories\n\n    # Identify highly variable genes\n    hvg_mask = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values\n    hvg_indices = np.where(hvg_mask)[0]\n\n    if len(hvg_indices) == 0:\n        print(\"No highly variable genes found for quantile normalization. Skipping.\")\n        return normalized_X\n\n    # Ensure we operate on a dense subset for quantile normalization for performance and simplicity\n    if issparse(normalized_X):\n        hvg_data\
    \ = normalized_X[:, hvg_indices].toarray()\n    else:\n        hvg_data = normalized_X[:, hvg_indices]\n\n    # Compute global reference distribution for HVGs\n    global_hvg_sorted = np.sort(hvg_data.flatten())\n\n    for batch in batches:\n        batch_mask = (batch_labels == batch)\n\n        if np.sum(batch_mask) == 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Extract HVG data for current batch\n        batch_hvg_data = hvg_data[batch_mask, :]\n\n        # Flatten, get sorted indices and values\n        original_shape = batch_hvg_data.shape\n        flat_batch_hvg = batch_hvg_data.flatten()\n\n        # Handle empty batches or batches with no HVGs\n        if flat_batch_hvg.size == 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Calculate ranks within the batch's HVG data\n        sorted_indices = np.argsort(flat_batch_hvg)\n        ranks = np.empty_like(sorted_indices)\n        ranks[sorted_indices] = np.arange(flat_batch_hvg.size)\n\n        # Map ranks to quantiles of the global reference\n \
    \       # Use linear interpolation if the sizes don't match\n        normalized_flat_batch_hvg = np.interp(ranks,\n                                              np.linspace(0, flat_batch_hvg.size - 1, global_hvg_sorted.size),\n                                              global_hvg_sorted)\n\n        # Reshape back and update the hvg_data array\n        hvg_data[batch_mask, :] = normalized_flat_batch_hvg.reshape(original_shape)\n\n    # Assign the normalized HVG data back to normalized_X\n    # Handle sparse matrix assignment properly\n    if issparse(normalized_X):\n        normalized_X = normalized_X.tolil()  # Convert to lil for efficient item assignment\n        for i, gene_idx in enumerate(hvg_indices):\n            normalized_X[:, gene_idx] = hvg_data[:, i].reshape(-1, 1)\n        normalized_X = normalized_X.tocsr()  # Convert back to csr\n    else:\n        normalized_X[:, hvg_indices] = hvg_data\n\n    return normalized_X\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: sc.AnnData)\
    \ -> sc.AnnData:\n    sc.set_figure_params(dpi=80, facecolor='white')\n    print(\"Aether II EtC-BRBG: Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization (Pre-PCA) initialized.\")\n\n    # Ensure normalized and log1p transformed\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata)\n\n    # Parameters\n    n_pca_components = 60 # From Daedalus II's SOTA (EID 378)\n    n_neighbors_graph = 48 # From Daedalus II's SOTA (EID 378)\n    random_state_val = 0\n\n    # --- Pre-processing for Embedding Path: Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization ---\n    print(\"Applying batch-specific quantile normalization on HVGs before PCA...\")\n    # Pass the full adata object instead of just adata.X\n    adata.X = _batch_specific_quantile_normalize(adata, adata.obs['batch'].astype('category'))\n    print(\"Batch-specific quantile normalization complete.\")\n\n    # --- Embedding Path: PCA -> ComBat ---\n    print(f\"Embedding Path: Running PCA (n={n_pca_components})\")\n    sc.tl.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=random_state_val)\n\
    \n    print(\"Running ComBat on PCs...\")\n    tmp_adata_combat = sc.AnnData(adata.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(tmp_adata_combat, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = tmp_adata_combat.X\n    print(f\"Embedding path complete. Final embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n\n    # --- Graph Path: Balanced kNN Graph on Integrated Embedding ---\n    print(f\"Graph Path: Building balanced kNN graph (n_neighbors={n_neighbors_graph}) on integrated embedding...\")\n    tmp_adata_graph = sc.AnnData(adata.obsm['X_emb'], obs=adata.obs)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(tmp_adata_graph, n_neighbors=n_neighbors_graph, use_rep='X', metric='cosine', random_state=random_state_val)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = tmp_adata_graph.obsp['connectivities']\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = tmp_adata_graph.obsp['distances']\n    print(\"Graph path complete.\")\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\n\
