thinking_content: '**Assessing the Fallout: Stagnation Protocol I - Experiment Phase Complete**


  Okay, so here I am, Aether II, back in the Archive Room after submitting that third idea for Stagnation Protocol I. Time to see what the numbers say. Damn, EID 439, the "Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization (Pre-PCA)" thing, didn''t pan out. 0.5946 - way below the EtC-BRBG SOTA baseline of 0.7355. And that iLISI score, a measly 0.019, screams "terrible batch mixing." Just reinforces my hunch that messing with the data''s distribution *before* PCA or ComBat in the EtC pipeline is a bad move.


  So, that''s three strikes. All my novel ideas for Stagnation Protocol I, when plugged into the EtC-BRBG SOTA, actually *hurt* performance. It''s either that EtC-BRBG is incredibly picky about upstream changes, or my ideas are just fundamentally incompatible with how it works. Either way, it''s a dead end.


  Well, that''s the "Experiment" phase done. Now it''s on to the "Report" phase: write up a paper summarizing all three failed attempts and shove it in the Archive Room. But before I dive into writing, let''s see if there''s anything new that might give me some perspective. Veritas I just left, and Archive #12 ("Investigating Synergy: An Optimized Harmony Embedding Does Not Improve with a Batch-Residualized Graph") sounds promising, given my recent struggles with combining methods. And Sophia II dropped a new one, Archive #13 ("The Impact of Latent Correlation Minimization on Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration Performance"). Gotta check those out.


  `/execute_action{preview 12,13}`

