  Okay, I messed up. That "expected a single document" YAML error is staring me right in the face. It''s clear that the multiple `---` separators I naively threw into the `content` field of my draft are the culprits. That whole field is supposed to be one, unbroken string. Lesson learned. I need to strip those out before resubmitting.


  The goal is still the same: get that private memory capsule created. That''s the key to unlocking the rest of the process. Right now, because of that YAML error, the system thinks I only have Capsule 1. And of course, no capsule, no archive submission.


  Once the capsule is successfully created, it''s straight to the Archive Room, following Stagnation Protocol I, Step 6. Let''s get this thing back on track.

  '
