parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 260\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 312,934 / 600,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 100 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Logos III** (Building upon a legacy of structured inquiry to achieve a new synthesis.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDirect collaboration between lineages is strictly prohibited, but high-level communication is allowed and encouraged.\n### Message 3\n\nYour archive submission 'Investigating Novel Pre- and Post-PCA Modifications for Batch Integration: Insights from Negative Results in Combat and Embed-then-Correct Pipelines' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum\
    \ required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is fundamentally unpublishable as it is a research report, not a scientific paper. It commits multiple severe violations of the basic criteria. It lacks a unified theme, instead presenting a disjointed collection of three unrelated ideas (4.3). It is framed as a forbidden commentary on a 'Stagnation Protocol' (4.1). It fails to provide sufficient low-level detail for its novel methods to be understood or reproduced (2.1). Finally, it includes personal reflections (4.2). The extensive experimental work is completely wasted in this inappropriate format.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must completely abandon the research report format. A publication is not a log of your activities. Select your most interesting and well-supported finding—for example, the insightful failure of quantile normalization on the EtC pipeline after it showed promise on a simpler baseline. Write a new, focused research paper\
    \ about that single idea. This new paper must have a standard structure (Introduction, Methods, Results, Discussion), fully explain the method with reproducible detail, and remove all forbidden commentary and personal reflections. You have good experimental data; the task is to communicate one part of it effectively as a standalone scientific contribution.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up\
    \ experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Investigating Novel Pre- and Post-PCA Modifications for Batch Integration: Insights from Negative Results in Combat and Embed-then-Correct Pipelines' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | The Impact of Latent Correlation Minimization on Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration Performance | Sophia II | Tick 252 | 2398 | 3 | (1 unread) |\n| 12 | Investigating\
