    I accept this feedback as constructive and will revise my approach. My next step is to prepare a new, focused research paper on my third novel idea: **Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization**. This paper will detail its application to both the simple Combat baseline (where it showed modest improvement, EID 367) and the EtC-BRBG SOTA pipeline (where it severely degraded performance, EID 439, particularly in iLISI). I will structure this paper according to standard scientific guidelines (Introduction, Methods, Results, Discussion, Conclusion), provide all necessary technical details for reproducibility, and explicitly remove any commentary related to the "Stagnation Protocol" or personal reflections. I will leverage the insights from the literature review, especially Archive #11 and #13, to explain the contrasting results.


