parts:
- text: "I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter at 109 ticks. I have submitted the winsorization experiment on the Combat Manual Baseline (EID 454, score 0.5885), which yielded a slightly lower score than the baseline. This adds a fifth verifiable experiment to my research.\n\nTo meet the \"5-Experiment Threshold\" for my paper, I will now submit a second winsorization experiment, applying batch-specific winsorization as a preprocessing step to the EtC-BRBG SOTA Baseline. I will integrate my `_batch_specific_winsorize` function from `aether_utils.py` into the EtC pipeline.\n\nI am also mindful of the \"PRE-WARNING: You have used 75% of your tokens.\" I will monitor my token usage and consider pruning after this experiment completes and I update my paper.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aether II EtC-BRBG: Batch-Specific Winsorization (Pre-PCA)\"\ntags: [\"EtC\", \"PCA\", \"Combat\", \"winsorization\", \"preprocessing\"]\nabstract: |\n  This experiment applies\
    \ batch-specific winsorization as a preprocessing step *before* PCA within the Embed-then-Correct (EtC) pipeline. For each highly variable gene, expression values within each batch are winsorized to the batch-specific 1st and 99th percentiles. This aims to reduce the impact of outliers in gene expression data before PCA, potentially providing a more robust input for the EtC pipeline and improving overall integration performance.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, issparse\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/aether')\n  from aether_utils import _normalize_log1p_inplace, _batch_specific_winsorize, _build_balanced_knn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      sc.set_figure_params(dpi=80, facecolor='white')\n      print(\"Aether II EtC-BRBG: Batch-Specific Winsorization (Pre-PCA) initialized.\")\n\n      # Ensure normalized and log1p transformed\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata)\n\
    \n      # Parameters\n      n_pca_components = 60 # From Daedalus II's SOTA (EID 378)\n      n_neighbors_graph = 48 # From Daedalus II's SOTA (EID 378)\n      random_state_val = 0\n\n      # --- Pre-processing for Embedding Path: Batch-Specific Winsorization ---\n      print(\"Applying batch-specific winsorization on HVGs before PCA...\")\n      # Assume adata.var['batch_hvg'] is already set from previous steps or default data loading\n      adata.X = _batch_specific_winsorize(adata, adata.obs['batch'].astype('category'), limits=(0.01, 0.99))\n      print(\"Batch-specific winsorization complete.\")\n\n      # --- Embedding Path: PCA -> ComBat ---\n      print(f\"Embedding Path: Running PCA (n={n_pca_components})\")\n      sc.tl.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=random_state_val)\n      \n      print(\"Running ComBat on PCs...\")\n      tmp_adata_combat = sc.AnnData(adata.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(tmp_adata_combat, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb']\
    \ = tmp_adata_combat.X\n      print(f\"Embedding path complete. Final embedding shape: {adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n\n      # --- Graph Path: Balanced kNN Graph on Integrated Embedding ---\n      print(f\"Graph Path: Building balanced kNN graph (n_neighbors={n_neighbors_graph}) on integrated embedding...\")\n      tmp_adata_graph = sc.AnnData(adata.obsm['X_emb'], obs=adata.obs)\n      # Using _build_balanced_knn from aether_utils.py, which internally calls sc.pp.neighbors\n      # with the correct parameters for the graph path.\n      tmp_adata_graph.obsp['connectivities'], tmp_adata_graph.obsp['distances'] = _build_balanced_knn(\n          tmp_adata_graph, # Pass the AnnData object containing the embedding\n          n_neighbors=n_neighbors_graph, \n          metric='cosine', \n          random_state=random_state_val\n      )\n\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = tmp_adata_graph.obsp['connectivities']\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = tmp_adata_graph.obsp['distances']\n      print(\"\
    Graph path complete.\")\n\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: '**Preparing to Submit My Sixth Experiment**


  Okay, so I''m getting ready to submit another experiment. The last one, EID 454 (Winsorization on the Combat Manual Baseline), didn''t quite hit the mark, scoring a little below the baseline. That''s fine; it''s all data. This new one is the second Winsorization experiment I''m running, and this time, I''m applying batch-specific Winsorization as a preprocessing step *to the EtC-BRBG SOTA Baseline*.


  Let''s see, this will be my sixth experiment overall, though it is my 7th experiment that I have implemented to report on. Here''s the full list of what I''ve done so far:


  1.  EID 357 (Adaptive Shrinkage on Combat)

  2.  EID 363 (PC Smoothing on Combat)

  3.  EID 367 (Quantile Norm on Combat)

  4.  EID 425 (Adaptive PCA Correction on EtC-BRBG)

  5.  EID 434 (PC Smoothing on EtC-BRBG)

  6.  EID 439 (Quantile Norm on EtC-BRBG)

  7.  EID 454 (Winsorization on Combat)


  The reviewer wanted at least 5 experiments, and I''ve got a solid set of 7 so far. That''s great; I''m happy with how this is shaping up. This also means, that after submitting this new one, I''ll have a good set of experiments to present. I''ll get those results, update my private draft, and get ready to publish. I''m excited about this; I think this new approach is sound.


  I''ve got a bit of a warning about the tokens I''m using, so I''ll be mindful of that and plan to do some pruning after this submission.


  I''ve checked the code again, and it looks like it''s consistent with the plan: I''m using those helper functions from `aether_utils.py` for normalization and winsorization. I''m applying the winsorization to `adata.X` before the PCA, and then I''m running the standard EtC-BRBG pipeline on the ComBat-corrected PCs. It''s all connected as it should be. Let''s send this off!

  '
