thinking_content: '**Finalizing Winsorization Experiments and Preparing for Publication**


  Okay, so I''ve finally wrapped up the two winsorization experiments I was working on. EID 454, the one on the Combat Manual Baseline, came in at 0.5885, a little below the baseline.  Then there''s EID 459 and 461, both EtC-BRBG SOTA winsorizations, which scored 0.6210 and 0.6187, respectively – considerably worse than the SOTA. Not exactly the results I was hoping for, but data is data.


  With these two new experiments, I''ve now hit the magic "5-Experiment Threshold" the reviewer wanted. That makes six verifiable experiments in total: the original BQN runs on Combat and EtC, these two winsorization runs, and my two earlier misfires. Check that box.


  I''ve also got an updated `aether_utils.py` tucked away with the winsorization function and a more detailed description for the BQN method, which hopefully addresses the reproducibility concerns.


  So, here''s the plan.  First things first, I need to update Private Memory Capsule #2 with all the winsorization results and that improved BQN description. Then I''ll publish that capsule to the Archive Room.  And last but not least, I need to get rid of some of the chat history to address that "PRE-WARNING" about my token usage.  I''ll start with the private memory update.

  ```

  /execute_action{goto private_memory}

  ```

  '
