thinking_content: "**Diagnostic Experiment & Aether Utils Update**\n\nOkay, so I've just been reviewing the code in `aether_utils.py` and I'm ready to move forward. The reviewer's suggestion for Archive #15 has me thinking. Essentially, I'm going to set up a test to see how effectively two batch correction methods, BQN and BW, improve the separation of batches compared to a baseline PCA approach.\n\nMy plan for this involves creating a `test` function. This function will be using several libraries, so I'll need to import `scanpy`, `numpy`, `scipy.sparse`, `pandas`, `sklearn.decomposition.PCA`, `sklearn.linear_model.LogisticRegression`, and `sklearn.model_selection.train_test_split`. I'll also import the BQN and BW functions from the `aether_utils.py` file, which has caused me to pause, and I will be working on in this turn.\n\nFirst, I need to focus on a bug in the `_batch_specific_quantile_normalize` function in `aether_utils.py`.  It looks like there's an issue with the rank calculation.\
  \ The code is trying to use a global reference distribution, but the current rank calculation and interpolation aren't quite right, and that's going to affect the function's accuracy.\n\nI've already started to correct the code, and here's what I've got:\n\n```python\n        original_shape = batch_hvg_data.shape\n        flat_batch_hvg = batch_hvg_data.flatten()\n        \n        if flat_batch_hvg.size == 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Corrected ranking and interpolation\n        ranks = np.argsort(np.argsort(flat_batch_hvg)) # Get ranks correctly (0 to N-1)\n        \n        # Map these ranks to quantiles of the global HVG reference distribution\n        # The original code for interpolation was attempting to map ranks (0 to size-1) to quantiles of global_hvg_sorted (0 to size-1),\n        # but the linspace part for global_hvg_sorted.size is incorrect.\n        # It should map the ranks to the 'positions' in the global_hvg_sorted array.\n        \n        # Correct interpolation:\n\
  \        # 1. Scale ranks to be between 0 and 1\n        scaled_ranks = ranks / (flat_batch_hvg.size - 1) if flat_batch_hvg.size > 1 else np.array([0.0])\n        # 2. Map scaled ranks to indices of the global sorted array\n        global_indices = scaled_ranks * (global_hvg_sorted.size - 1) if global_hvg_sorted.size > 1 else np.array([0.0])\n        \n        # 3. Perform linear interpolation using these indices\n        normalized_flat_batch_hvg = np.interp(global_indices, \n                                              np.arange(global_hvg_sorted.size), \n                                              global_hvg_sorted)\n        \n        hvg_data[batch_mask, :] = normalized_flat_batch_hvg.reshape(original_shape)\n```\nEssentially, I'm making the following changes: the ranking calculation is corrected. The logic for the interpolation is cleaned up.\n\nNow, with this fix in place, I want to commit this updated `aether_utils.py` to my storage. In the next turn, I'll return to the diagnostic\
  \ experiment I was planning.\n"
