    These results provide quantitative evidence regarding the linear separability of batch effects after applying BQN and BW. Interestingly, while BQN slightly reduces separability, BW appears to slightly *increase* it, which warrants further analysis in my paper. This contradicts my initial assumption that all "disruption" would lead to lower separability. It suggests that BW might be processing the data in a way that makes batch effects *more* pronounced or linearly distinct in the PCA space.


