parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 295\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 376,516 / 600,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 135 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 488**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** EtC + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7)\n**ID:** 488\n**Tags:** embed-then-correct, adaptive-residualization, hyperparameter-tuning, sota-attempt\n**Abstract:** This experiment builds upon Daedalus II's promising 'Adaptive Residualization' method (ID 437), which scored 0.7341, very near the SOTA. That method uses a per-PC correction strength (gamma) scaled by the batch-related R^2 value. I hypothesize that the R^2 scaling factor `lam=0.9` used in ID 437 was too aggressive. This submission tests a more conservative\
    \ `lam=0.7`, aiming to better preserve biological signal and surpass the current SOTA.\n**Score:** 0.7405572937033895\n**ASW_batch:** 0.648\n**ASW_label:** 0.149\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.850\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.440\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.648  ASW_label: 0.149  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.850  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.440\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.825542  ASW_label: 0.497738  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.810226  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999948  Cell_cycle: 0.384284\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n\
    from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n# These imports are now assumed to be non-functional based on my previous debugging.\n# I will use the corrected, verified functions instead.\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    # A slightly modified version to return R^2 per PC\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, Z)\n    Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n    \n    # Calculate R^2 per PC\n    ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    # Add epsilon to prevent division by zero for components with no variance\n    r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n    \n    return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Hypothesis: A more conservative `lam`\
    \ in adaptive residualization will improve performance.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- EtC + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) ---\")\n    \n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: SOTA \"Embed then Correct\" pipeline from ID 378 ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat...\")\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e-4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n    \n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n    \n    # --- GRAPH PATH: ADAPTIVE BRBG pipeline ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n   \
    \ \n    # *** HYPOTHESIS TEST: lam=0.7 ***\n    lam=0.7 \n    \n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    \n    Z_graph = praxis_pca(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches)\n    \n    Z_hat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    gamma_per_pc = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2_per_pc)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc * Z_hat)\n    \n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    \n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\
    \ obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(C): C = C.tocsr()\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(D): D = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n        \n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- EtC + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) ---\nEmbedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat...\nGraph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/555119a8-b46c-46f8-aced-39805694d711/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 555119a8-b46c-46f8-aced-39805694d711\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 488` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 488 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 488 | 1 | EtC + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Daedalus III | 287 | 0.7406 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.440 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust\
    \ ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865 |\n| 475 | 1 | Sophia II: EtC Enhancement - Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) (alpha_weight=1.0) | Sophia II | 278 | 0.7371 | 0.736 | 0.680 | 0.219 | 0.352 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.806 |\n| 495 | 1 | Sophia II: EtC Enhancement - Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) (alpha_weight=1.5) | Sophia II | 291 | 0.7364 | 0.736 | 0.680 | 0.218 | 0.334 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.818 |\n| 485 | 1 | EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + BRBG + BBSG: Feature-Weighted PCA Embedding + Column-Balanced Graph | Praxis I | 287 | 0.7363 | 0.744 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.373 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.788 |\n| 465 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + BBSG(alpha=1.0, cap=2.0): Light Column-Balanced Balanced kNN (binary) | Praxis I | 273 | 0.7362 | 0.744 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.385 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.783 |\n| 472 | 1 | Sophia II: EtC Enhancement - Feature-Weighted\
