tick: 309
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 309\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 180,559 / 600,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 149 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 508**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ablation R1: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + BRBG(lam=0.7) + BBSG (binary)\n**ID:** 508\n**Tags:** ablation, residualization, lam-0.7, embed-then-correct, bbsg, fwpca\n**Abstract:** Isolate the effect of stronger batch residualization by reducing lam from 0.9 to 0.7 in BRBG while keeping the rest identical to the strong baseline: EtC embedding with FWPCA α=0.5 and BBSG binary graph (k=48, cosine). Hypothesis: slightly stronger shrinkage of batch-predictable variance improves overall score without harming label structure.\n**Score:**\
    \ 0.7229466687214896\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.725\n**NMI:** 0.676\n**Graph_conn:** 0.956\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.896\n**cLISI:** 0.951\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.725  NMI: 0.676\n  Graph_conn: 0.956  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.896  cLISI: 0.951\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.724918  NMI: 0.676349\n  Graph_conn: 0.956977  kBET: 0.753959  iLISI: 0.896184  cLISI: 0.985810\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n\
    \        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    Zhat = B @ W\n    return Zhat\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config: match strong baseline except lam\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n\
    \    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.7  # residualization schedule ablation (baseline 0.9)\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    alpha_weight = 0.5  # FWPCA α=0.5 per strong prior result\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Embedding: FWPCA (var^{-α/2} scaling) → PCA60 → ComBat on PC scores\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n    Xd = Xd.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_weight).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * w\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization (lam=0.7) → BBSG (binary)\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, alpha=1.0, cap=2.0)\n    if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n    \
    \    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg  # binary by design\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/f6120c69-16b8-43b3-8c62-a472185a6df3/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: f6120c69-16b8-43b3-8c62-a472185a6df3\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7)' (ID: 515) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7414041826905106\n**ASW_batch:** 0.664\n**ASW_label:** 0.111\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.859\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:**\
