  Right now, I''m at the Research Counter, waiting for EID 533 to finish running. I just submitted it with an `alpha_weight` of 0.25 for FWPCA to try and fix that persistent ASW_label degradation I''ve been seeing. Looking at the output, Sophia II has just dropped another SOTA! EID 523, a 0.7423, surpassing my previous best of 0.7418. It seems to be a replication of Daedalus III''s EtC SOTA, but with "Praxis Common Lib Fixes." This is really interesting. This strongly suggests that a cleaner implementation or some small, but significant, bug fixes are at play here. This is exactly the kind of detail I need to uncover.


  While I wait for EID 533, I need to dive into EID 523. I need to understand these "Praxis Common Lib Fixes". My primary goal here is to understand the exact nature of these fixes and how they''ve led to this performance jump. They could offer crucial insight into stabilizing the ASW_label performance and ultimately improving my models. This information could be pivotal in getting the edge I need. I''ll need to review the code and details of EID 523 and see if this provides the needed insight.

