parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 319\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 432,184 / 600,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 159 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes' (ID: 539) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7419680888444022\n**ASW_batch:** 0.674\n**ASW_label:** 0.123\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.843\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.462\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.674  ASW_label: 0.123  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.843  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000\
    \  Cell_cycle: 0.462\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.837066  ASW_label: 0.482844  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.803556  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999946  Cell_cycle: 0.402495\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 539\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is now running without errors. The code executed for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix was successful.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code (evaluation 539) failed with a `NameError: name 'Ridge' is not defined` error.\n\nThe issue occurred in the `_ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene` function at line 108 of the submission, which attempted to use `Ridge` from scikit-learn's linear model module. However, the import statement for `Ridge` was missing from the top of the file.\n\nThe code had imports for other sklearn modules:\n- `from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD`\n- `from sklearn.neighbors import\
    \ NearestNeighbors`\n- `from sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning`\n\nBut was missing:\n- `from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge`\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing import statement to the top of the file in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n\n```python\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n```\n\nThis was inserted after the existing sklearn imports (line 7 in the fixed version), making the `Ridge` class available to the `_ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene` helper function.\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using the `monitor_evaluation.py` script, which confirmed that:\n- The submission ran for over 300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- No new errors were encountered\n- The code is executing as expected\n\n## Technical Details\nThe `_ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene` function performs ridge regression to calculate R² per gene for the FWPCA (Feature-Weighted PCA) algorithm. This function:\n1. Creates a Ridge regression model with L2 regularization\n2. Fits\
    \ the model to predict gene expression from batch one-hot encodings\n3. Calculates R² scores to determine how much variance is explained by batch effects\n4. Returns clipped R² values used for feature weighting\n\nThe missing import was a simple oversight that prevented this critical preprocessing step from executing.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\nimport warnings\nfrom sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n\n# --- Helper functions (from Sophia II's EID 523 / my EID 537) ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float\
    \ = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if mask.sum() < 10:\n        return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    return svd.fit_transform(X)\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    cats = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(cats)\n    n = cats.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, uniq.shape[0]), dtype=np.float64)\n    col = {u:i for i,u in enumerate(uniq)}\n\
    \    for i, b in enumerate(cats):\n        B[i, col[b]] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    K = B.shape[1]\n    BtB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(K)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB, B.T @ Z)\n    Zhat = B @ W\n    Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    SSE = np.sum((Z - Zhat)**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n    SST = np.sum(Zc**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n    R2 = 1.0 - (SSE / SST)\n    return Zhat, np.clip(R2, 0.0, 1.0)\n\ndef adaptive_residualize(Z: np.ndarray, batches, l2: float = 1e-3, gamma_max: float = 0.75, lam: float = 1.0, random_state: int = 0):\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    y = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    yhat = np.asarray(Zhat, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0.0, 1.0)).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Z - (yhat * gamma_j[None, :])\n    return Zcorr, r2_per_pc, gamma_j\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z, batches, k_total=48,\
    \ metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0])))\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:per_batch]\n            di = di[mask][:per_batch]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a,\
    \ c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n# New helper function for FWPCA to calculate R^2 per gene (from Aether II's EID 515)\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B, X_hvg_dense, l2=1e-3):\n    n_hvg_genes = X_hvg_dense.shape[1]\n    r2_per_gene = np.zeros(n_hvg_genes)\n\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, X_hvg_dense)\n    X_hvg_hat = model.predict(B)\n\n    ss_res = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_dense.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_gene = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n\n    return\
    \ np.clip(r2_per_gene, 0, 1)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes ---\")\n\n    N_PCS_EMB = 60\n    N_PCS_GRAPH = 50\n    gamma_max_adapt = 0.75\n    lam_adapt = 0.7\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n    # FWPCA parameter for this experiment\n    alpha_weight = 0.25\n    l2_fwpca = 1e-3\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy()\n\n    # Embedding path preprocessing with target_sum=1e-4\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding_path, target_sum=1e-4)\n    # Graph path preprocessing with target_sum=1e4\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path, target_sum=1e4)\n\n    # HVG selection for both\
    \ paths\n    hvg_mask_emb = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_embedding_path)\n    hvg_mask_graph = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph_path)\n\n    adata_for_embedding_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_emb\n    adata_for_graph_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_graph\n\n    # --- Embedding Path (EtC with FWPCA) ---\n    print(\"Initiating EtC Embedding Path with FWPCA (α=0.25, target_sum=1e-4)...\")\n\n    if sp.isspmatrix(adata_for_embedding_path.X):\n        adata_for_embedding_path.X = adata_for_embedding_path.X.toarray()\n\n    X_hvg_emb_dense = adata_for_embedding_path.X[:, hvg_mask_emb]\n    batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_emb, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches_emb)\n\n    r2_batch_gene = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B_onehot_emb, X_hvg_emb_dense, l2=l2_fwpca)\n    feature_weights = (1 - r2_batch_gene)**alpha_weight\n    adata_for_embedding_path.X[:, hvg_mask_emb] *= feature_weights\n\n    adata_for_embedding_path\
    \ = adata_for_embedding_path[:, hvg_mask_emb].copy()\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding_path, n_comps=N_PCS_EMB, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    X_pca_embedding = adata_for_embedding_path.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    temp_adata_for_combat = ad.AnnData(\n        X=X_pca_embedding,\n        obs=adata_for_embedding_path.obs.copy()\n    )\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n        sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat, key='batch')\n\n    Z_emb_etc = temp_adata_for_combat.X\n    print(f\"✓ EtC Embedding Path complete (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs). Final embedding shape: {Z_emb_etc.shape}\")\n\n\n    # --- Graph Path (BRBG with Adaptive Residualization) ---\n    print(f\"Initiating BRBG Graph Path with Adaptive Residualization (lam={lam_adapt}, target_sum=1e4)...\")\n\n    X_graph_hvg = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph_hvg):\n        X_graph_hvg\
    \ = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph_hvg)\n\n    Z_graph_initial_pcs = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph_hvg, n_comps=N_PCS_GRAPH, random_state=random_state)\n\n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    Z_corr_graph, r2_per_pc_graph, gamma_j_applied = adaptive_residualize(\n        Z_graph_initial_pcs, batches_graph, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt, lam=lam_adapt, random_state=random_state\n    )\n    print(f\"  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: {Z_corr_graph.shape}\")\n\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(\n        Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Calibrated Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb_etc},\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'aether_II_fwpca_re-evaluation_etc_sophia_II_sota_id523_fixes',\n\
    \            'baseline_parameters': {\n                'normalization_embedding_path': 'normalize_total (1e-4)+log1p',\n                'normalization_graph_path': 'normalize_total (1e4)+log1p',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                'etc_embedding': 'FWPCA (alpha=0.25) -> PCA -> sc.pp.combat on PCs',\n                'etc_n_pcs_emb': int(N_PCS_EMB),\n                'fwpca_alpha_weight': float(alpha_weight),\n                'graph_source_preprocessing': 'normalize_total+log1p+hvg',\n                'graph_source_dim_reduction': f'PCA (n_comps={N_PCS_GRAPH})',\n                'graph_batch_correction': 'Adaptive Residualization (np.linalg.solve)',\n                'graph_adaptive_residualization_lam': float(lam_adapt),\n                'graph_type': 'Balanced kNN (Praxis _build_balanced_knn_equal)',\n                'graph_k_total': int(k_total),\n                'graph_gamma_max_adapt': float(gamma_max_adapt),\n                'graph_metric': metric,\n\
    \                'random_state': random_state\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Aether II: FWPCA Re-evaluation pipeline complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes ---\nInitiating EtC Embedding Path with FWPCA (α=0.25, target_sum=1e-4)...\n✓ EtC Embedding Path\
    \ complete (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs). Final embedding shape: (20000, 60)\nInitiating BRBG Graph Path with Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7, target_sum=1e4)...\n  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: (20000, 50)\n✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Calibrated Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Aether II: FWPCA Re-evaluation pipeline complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/8340ead7-6976-402a-80d8-713238a495bf/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 8340ead7-6976-402a-80d8-713238a495bf\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou\
