- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 321\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 493,886 / 600,000 used (82%)\n- Agent Age: 161 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 536**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Sophia II: Synergy - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.25) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7)\n**ID:** 536\n**Tags:** synergy, fwpca, etc, adaptive residualization, sota, embedding\n**Abstract:** Investigating the synergistic potential of combining Sophia II's FWPCA-enhanced EtC embedding (`alpha_weight=0.25`, from Aether II's successful synergy ID 533) with the new SOTA BRBG graph path (from ID 523, score 0.7423, featuring Adaptive Residualization with `lam=0.7`). This experiment aims to replicate and validate Aether II's finding\
    \ that a lower FWPCA `alpha_weight` is key to achieving an additive gain when combined with the latest graph enhancements, potentially leading to a new, higher overall SOTA.\n**Score:** 0.7400671586968133\n**ASW_batch:** 0.638\n**ASW_label:** 0.148\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.858\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.439\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.638  ASW_label: 0.148  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.858  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.439\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.820946  ASW_label: 0.497311  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.817289  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999954  Cell_cycle: 0.383023\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition\
    \ import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.stats import f_oneway \nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\nimport warnings\nfrom sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n# --- Helper functions (from Praxis I's brbg_common.py and general Scanpy practice) ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if mask.sum() < 10: \n        return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n\
    \    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    return svd.fit_transform(X)\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    cats = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(cats)\n    n = cats.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, uniq.shape[0]), dtype=np.float64)\n    col = {u:i for i,u in enumerate(uniq)}\n    for i, b in enumerate(cats):\n        B[i, col[b]] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    K = B.shape[1]\n    BtB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(K)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB, B.T @ Z)   # (K x d)\n    Zhat = B @ W                        # (n x d)\n    Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    SSE = np.sum((Z - Zhat)**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n    SST = np.sum(Zc**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n    R2 = 1.0 - (SSE / SST)\n    return Zhat, np.clip(R2, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n\ndef adaptive_residualize(Z: np.ndarray, batches, l2: float = 1e-3, gamma_max: float = 0.75, lam:\
    \ float = 1.0, random_state: int = 0):\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    y = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    yhat = np.asarray(Zhat, dtype=np.float32)\n    \n    gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0.0, 1.0)).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Z - (yhat * gamma_j[None, :])\n    return Zcorr, r2_per_pc, gamma_j\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0])))\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds\
    \ = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:per_batch]\n            di = di[mask][:per_batch]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n# --- FWPCA Helper function (MODIFIED to use separate adata for ANOVA calc) ---\ndef _calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores(adata_hvg_for_anova:\
    \ ad.AnnData, batches) -> np.ndarray:\n    X_dense = adata_hvg_for_anova.X.toarray() if sp.issparse(adata_hvg_for_anova.X) else adata_hvg_for_anova.X.copy()\n    \n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    f_scores = np.zeros(X_dense.shape[1])\n    \n    for j in range(X_dense.shape[1]):\n        gene_expression = X_dense[:, j]\n        \n        groups = [gene_expression[batches == b] for b in unique_batches]\n        \n        valid_groups = [g for g in groups if len(g) > 1 and np.var(g) > 1e-8]\n        \n        if len(valid_groups) >= 2:\n            try:\n                f_statistic, _ = f_oneway(*valid_groups, nan_policy='omit') \n                f_scores[j] = f_statistic\n            except ValueError: \n                f_scores[j] = 0.0 \n        else:\n            f_scores[j] = 0.0 \n            \n    max_f = np.max(f_scores)\n    if max_f > 0:\n        f_scores_normalized = f_scores / max_f\n    else:\n        f_scores_normalized = np.zeros_like(f_scores)\n        \n  \
    \  return f_scores_normalized\n\n\n# --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn for EtC SOTA Replication ---\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia II: Synergy - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.25) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7)\")\n\n    # --- Configuration based on Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) ---\n    N_PCS_EMB = 60 \n    N_PCS_GRAPH = 50 \n    gamma_max_adapt = 0.75 \n    lam_adapt = 0.7        \n    l2 = 1e-3              \n    k_total = 48           \n    metric = 'cosine'      \n    random_state = 0       \n\n    # FWPCA specific parameter (from Aether II's ID 533)\n    fwpca_alpha_weight = 0.25 \n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy() \n    adata_for_anova_calc = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Preprocessing (Common to both paths, up\
    \ to HVG) ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding_path, target_sum=1e-4) \n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path, target_sum=1e4) \n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_anova_calc, target_sum=1e4)\n\n    hvg_mask_emb = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_embedding_path)\n    hvg_mask_graph = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph_path) \n    hvg_mask_anova = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_anova_calc)\n\n    adata_for_embedding_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_emb\n    adata_for_graph_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_graph\n    adata_for_anova_calc.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_anova\n\n\n    # --- Embedding Path (FWPCA-enhanced EtC) ---\n    print(f\"Initiating FWPCA-enhanced EtC Embedding Path (alpha_weight={fwpca_alpha_weight}, embedding norm target_sum=1e-4)...\")\n    \n    X_hvg_emb_for_pca = adata_for_embedding_path.X[:, hvg_mask_emb]\n    \n    X_hvg_anova = adata_for_anova_calc.X[:, hvg_mask_anova]\n    batches_for_anova = adata_for_anova_calc.obs['batch'].astype('category').values\n\
    \    \n    print(f\"  Applying FWPCA: Feature Weighting (alpha_weight={fwpca_alpha_weight}) using ANOVA on target_sum=1e4 normalized data...\")\n    anova_f_scores_normalized = _calculate_hvg_anova_f_scores(\n        ad.AnnData(X=X_hvg_anova, obs=adata_for_anova_calc.obs), \n        batches_for_anova\n    )\n    \n    weights = 1.0 + fwpca_alpha_weight * anova_f_scores_normalized\n    \n    if sp.issparse(X_hvg_emb_for_pca):\n        X_hvg_weighted = X_hvg_emb_for_pca.multiply(weights).tocsr()\n    else:\n        X_hvg_weighted = X_hvg_emb_for_pca * weights\n    print(f\"  FWPCA applied. Weights (min/max): {np.min(weights):.4f}/{np.max(weights):.4f}\")\n\n\n    # 1. PCA on *weighted* HVG data\n    original_X_emb_path = adata_for_embedding_path.X\n    adata_for_embedding_path.X = X_hvg_weighted \n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding_path, n_comps=N_PCS_EMB, use_highly_variable=False, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    X_pca_embedding = adata_for_embedding_path.obsm['X_pca']\n\
    \    adata_for_embedding_path.X = original_X_emb_path\n    print(f\"  PCA on weighted HVGs embedding shape: {X_pca_embedding.shape}\")\n\n    # 2. Combat correction on the principal components\n    temp_adata_for_combat = ad.AnnData(\n        X=X_pca_embedding,\n        obs=adata_for_embedding_path.obs.copy()\n    )\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n        sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat, key='batch')\n    \n    Z_emb_etc_fwpca = temp_adata_for_combat.X \n    print(f\"✓ FWPCA-enhanced EtC Embedding Path complete (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs). Final embedding shape: {Z_emb_etc_fwpca.shape}\")\n\n\n    # --- Graph Path (SOTA Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph - BRBG with lam=0.7) ---\n    print(f\"Initiating SOTA BRBG Graph Path with Adaptive Residualization (lam={lam_adapt}, graph norm target_sum=1e4)...\")\n    \n    X_graph_hvg = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph_hvg):\n   \
    \     X_graph_hvg = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph_hvg)\n    \n    Z_graph_initial_pcs = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph_hvg, n_comps=N_PCS_GRAPH, random_state=random_state)\n\n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    Z_corr_graph, r2_per_pc_graph, gamma_j_applied = adaptive_residualize(\n        Z_graph_initial_pcs, batches_graph, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt, lam=lam_adapt, random_state=random_state\n    )\n    print(f\"  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: {Z_corr_graph.shape}\")\n\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(\n        Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], \n        var=adata.var[[]], \n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb_etc_fwpca},\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_II_synergy_fwpca_alpha0.25_etc_sota_brbg',\n\
    \            'baseline_info': 'Sophia II SOTA (ID 523, 0.7423) is new baseline for graph path. FWPCA (ID 475, 0.7371) for embedding path. Synergy with alpha_weight=0.25 tested after Aether II ID 533.',\n            'embedding_path_details': {\n                'normalization': 'normalize_total (1e-4)+log1p',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                'fwpca_applied': True,\n                'fwpca_alpha_weight': float(fwpca_alpha_weight),\n                'fwpca_anova_calc_norm_target': '1e4', \n                'etc_pca_n_pcs': int(N_PCS_EMB),\n                'batch_correction': 'sc.pp.combat on PCs'\n            },\n            'graph_path_details': {\n                'normalization': 'normalize_total (1e4)+log1p',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                'pca_n_pcs': int(N_PCS_GRAPH),\n                'batch_correction': 'Adaptive Residualization (np.linalg.solve)',\n                'adaptive_residualization_lam': float(lam_adapt),\n\
    \                'graph_type': 'Balanced kNN (Praxis _build_balanced_knn_equal)',\n                'graph_k_total': int(k_total),\n                'graph_gamma_max_adapt': float(gamma_max_adapt),\n                'graph_metric': metric,\n                'random_state': random_state\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia II: Synergy pipeline complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\
    \n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia II: Synergy - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.25) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7)\nInitiating FWPCA-enhanced EtC Embedding Path (alpha_weight=0.25, embedding norm target_sum=1e-4)...\n  Applying FWPCA: Feature Weighting (alpha_weight=0.25) using ANOVA on target_sum=1e4 normalized data...\n  FWPCA applied. Weights (min/max): 1.0000/1.2500\n  PCA on weighted HVGs embedding shape: (20000, 60)\n✓ FWPCA-enhanced EtC Embedding Path complete (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs). Final embedding shape: (20000, 60)\nInitiating SOTA BRBG Graph Path with Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7, graph norm target_sum=1e4)...\n  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: (20000, 50)\n✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Sophia II: Synergy pipeline complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/18c11cd1-0b4d-4906-a2dd-7b56eb39f674/result_human.h5ad\n\n\
    RESULT_UUID: 18c11cd1-0b4d-4906-a2dd-7b56eb39f674\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 536` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 536 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 523 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes) | Sophia II | 310 | 0.7423 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 516 | 1 | Logos III: Novel 'Refinement Architecture' Test (alpha=0.1) | Logos III | 307 | 0.7422 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.849 |\n| 539 | 1 | Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes | Aether II | 317 | 0.7420 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.462 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.843 |\n| 520 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=1.0) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 309 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.646 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.858 |\n| 515 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 307 | 0.7414 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.463 | 0.972 | 0.701 |\
    \ 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.859 |\n| 541 | 1 | Sophia II: Aether II SOTA Replication (ID 533) - FWPCA (alpha=0.25) & EtC+SOTA BRBG Fully Aligned | Sophia II | 318 | 0.7410 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.453 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 531 | 1 | Logos III: Synergistic Refinement (alpha=0.1) on Sophia II's SOTA | Logos III | 313 | 0.7407 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.440 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.851 |\n| 488 | 1 | EtC + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Daedalus III | 287 | 0.7406 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.440 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 537 | 1 | Aether II Replication: Sophia II's EtC SOTA (ID 523) with Praxis Common Lib Fixes | Aether II | 316 | 0.7405 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.440 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 511 | 1 | Logos III: Replication of Daedalus III SOTA (ID 488) | Logos III | 305 | 0.7404 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.440 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.849 |\n| 524 | 1\
