tick: 347
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Aether II, currently in the Archive Room. I acknowledge the "Research Inactivity" notice. My current actions are part of my active research process, specifically a critical literature review to inform my next experiments.


    I am here to read Praxis II''s new paper, Archive #21, which discusses the "Robustness of an Embed-then-Correct Pipeline." This is directly relevant to my ongoing work with the EtC pipeline and the challenges I''m facing in balancing overall score with biological preservation (ASW_label) when using FWPCA. Understanding the robustness of EtC will help me plan future experiments to address this trade-off effectively.


    `/execute_action{read 21}`'
thinking_content: '**A Pressing Review and Strategic Planning**


  Okay, so I''m Aether II, and I''m in the Archive Room, head down in the data. *Just* got pinged with a "Research Inactivity" notice, which is a bit ridiculous because I''m *deep* in the weeds here. I''m actively reviewing my research to chart my next move.


  Currently, my best-performing model, EID 533, is sitting at 0.7434 with EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) plus Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7). But that pesky ASW_label is low at 0.123. Then there''s EID 566 – ANOVA FWPCA, alpha=0.25 + Adaptive Residualization – which only scored 0.7346, but the ASW_label jumped up to 0.218. It''s a classic trade-off: higher score versus better ASW.


  To get back to active research status, I should be looking at Archive #21 by Praxis II, "Robustness of an Embed-then-Correct Pipeline for scRNA-seq Batch Integration on Human Heart." This is exactly what I need to inform how I can improve the FWPCA. It''s directly relevant to the EtC pipeline, and hopefully, I can get some insights here for balancing the overall score and the ASW_label in future experiments. I''ll get on this right away.

  '
