role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 361\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 367,546 / 600,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 201 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 593**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** BRBG + Density-Adaptive BBSG (±15% cross-batch quotas by local density)\n**ID:** 593\n**Tags:** bbsg, balanced-graph, density-adaptive, residualization, embed-then-correct\n**Abstract:** We extend BBSG by allocating per-cell cross-batch quotas based on local density in Zcorr (distance to 30th NN): dense regions get slightly more cross-batch edges; sparse/border regions get fewer, preserving labels. We keep graphs binary and write true distances. BRBG residualization unchanged (λ=0.9, γ_max=0.74, PCA50). Hypothesis:\
    \ improve mixing where safe while protecting boundaries.\n**Score:** 0.7334599037588598\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.760\n**NMI:** 0.710\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.930\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.760  NMI: 0.710\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.930  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.759957  NMI: 0.709834\n  Graph_conn: 0.946873  kBET: 0.752744  iLISI: 0.929825  cLISI: 0.990044\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    from scipy import sparse as sp\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n\
    \    # Build directed matrices\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    # Symmetrize: connectivity by max; distances by max to ensure presence both ways\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym, D_sym\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    delta = 0.15          # ±15% modulation of cross-batch fraction\n    k_density = 30        # local density proxy\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3',\
    \ batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches_cat = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    batches = np.asarray(batches_cat.values)\n    batch_codes = batches_cat.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n    n = adata.n_obs\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n\n    # Embedding: variance-weighted PCA -> ComBat (EtC path, for analysis only)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n    Xd = Xd.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * 0.5).astype(np.float32)  # α=0.5\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X,\
    \ dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph representation: PCA50 -> adaptive residualization -> Zcorr\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Local density proxy: distance to k_density-th NN in Zcorr (all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]  # distance to k-th neighbor (exclude self via +1 above)\n    # Map small distance (dense) -> higher cross-batch fraction\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k)\
    \ + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)            # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))            # e.g., 0.75 with 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta                # in [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)      # safety bounds\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances (fixed upper bounds)\n    # Maximum cross-batch per other batch (worst case f_cross=0.9): ceil(0.9*k/(B-1))\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))          # worst case within\n    nn_models = {}\n    train_indices = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        train_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n \
    \       nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    # For each batch model, query all cells\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii  # indices in the local (per-batch) training set\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(batch_codes[i])\n        # quotas\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch neighbors\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        # drop self if present (distance 0)\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(train_indices[bi][ii[start:start\
    \ + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch neighbors\n        # distribute remainder to batches with smallest first-neighbor distance\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        # score batches by their first neighbor distance for this i (smaller is closer)\n        batch_scores = []\n        for j in other_batches:\n            batch_scores.append((j, nn_dists[j][i][0]))\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(train_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\
    \n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.array(rows, dtype=np.int32),\n                                                     np.array(cols, dtype=np.int32),\n                                                     np.array(dvals, dtype=np.float32),\n                                                     n)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/575cdc7f-3fe3-4741-b918-9ea91700cc09/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 575cdc7f-3fe3-4741-b918-9ea91700cc09\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\
    \n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 593` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 593 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 550 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 2 -\
