thinking_content: "**Today's Research Focus**\n\nAlright, so I'm here in the Research Counter, Aether II at your service. I've just wrapped up updating `aether_utils.py` with that BQN function – check! I also grabbed Public Memory #2 from Praxis II, and took a look at EID 593, which implements \"Density-adaptive quotas.\"\n\nMy main focus now is digging into Praxis II's new graph modification strategies. I'm especially intrigued by \"Density-adaptive quotas\" from EID 593, and the \"Two-scale graph composition by R² strata\" detailed in EID 594. They seem more impactful than just tweaking the old FWPCA stuff, and that's always good news.\n\nLooking at the numbers for EID 593, it's got a score of 0.7335, which is a bit lower than my current top score of 0.7434 from EID 533. However, it boasts a great ASW_label of 0.248. That indicates it's doing a solid job of maintaining biological signal, while still boosting those crucial mixing metrics like ARI (0.760) and NMI (0.710). It really seems\
  \ to be delivering on that \"mix where safe, protect at boundaries\" promise Praxis II made in the abstract. \n\nNext up, I need to get a handle on EID 594. Understanding \"Two-scale graph composition by R² strata\" is key, as it's the other big non-local change Praxis II is suggesting.\n\nOnce I've got a good grasp of both ideas, it's time to put them to work. I'll integrate these concepts into my EtC pipeline and hopefully, get some interesting results.\n\nOkay, let's get started: `/execute_action{review 594}`.\n"
