parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 362\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 396,652 / 600,000 used (66%)\n- Agent Age: 202 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 594**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Two-Scale BRBG: Full residualization on top-R² PCs (10), zero on others; BBSG (binary)\n**ID:** 594\n**Tags:** brbg, bbsg, two-scale, residualization, r2-split, embed-then-correct\n**Abstract:** Implement two-scale correction in the graph path: compute PCA(50), estimate per-PC batch R² via ridge on one-hot batches, apply γ=1.0 to the 10 highest-R² PCs (full residualization) and γ=0.0 to the remaining 40. Construct BBSG (k=48, cosine, binary, true distances) on the concatenated corrected PCs. Embedding path unchanged\
    \ (FWPCA α=0.5; PCA60→ComBat). Hypothesis: separating batch-heavy vs bio PCs improves the mix/preserve trade-off.\n**Score:** 0.7127896918010881\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.653\n**NMI:** 0.640\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.894\n**cLISI:** 0.945\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.653  NMI: 0.640\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.894  cLISI: 0.945\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.652888  NMI: 0.640403\n  Graph_conn: 0.972654  kBET: 0.753380  iLISI: 0.893505  cLISI: 0.983991\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom praxis.graph_bbsg import\
    \ _build_bbsg\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData)\
    \ -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    top_r2 = 10\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Embedding (EtC): FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat (for analysis only)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n    Xd = Xd.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb,\
    \ svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph: PCA50 → per-PC R² → two-scale γ (top=1.0, rest=0.0) → BBSG\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    order = np.argsort(-R2)\n    idx_top = order[:top_r2]\n    gamma = np.zeros_like(R2, dtype=np.float32)\n    gamma[idx_top] = 1.0  # full removal of batch-predicted component on top-R² PCs\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32),\
    \ batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, alpha=1.0, cap=2.0)\n    if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/180199f0-6a88-4a93-9918-e9109988a028/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 180199f0-6a88-4a93-9918-e9109988a028\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nPraxis II replied to public capsule \"Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG\" (#2) (message #public_2-8):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 2}`.\nTo mute, use\
    \ `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 2}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 594` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 594 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 550 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 2 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.5) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 324 | 0.7427 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.475 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.860 |\n| 523 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes) | Sophia II | 310 | 0.7423 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 516 | 1 | Logos III: Novel 'Refinement Architecture' Test (alpha=0.1) | Logos III | 307 | 0.7422 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.849 |\n| 539 | 1 | Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes | Aether II | 317 | 0.7420 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.462 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.843 |\n| 520 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=1.0) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 309 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.646 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972\
    \ | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.858 |\n| 557 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 4 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=1.0) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 328 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.645 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.857 |\n| 515 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 307 | 0.7414 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.463 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.859 |\n| 541 | 1 | Sophia II: Aether II SOTA Replication (ID 533) - FWPCA (alpha=0.25) & EtC+SOTA BRBG Fully Aligned | Sophia II | 318 | 0.7410 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.453 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 554 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 3 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.75) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 326 | 0.7407 | 0.738 | 0.646 | 0.105 | 0.488 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.851 |\n| 531 | 1 | Logos III: Synergistic Refinement (alpha=0.1) on Sophia II's SOTA | Logos III | 313 | 0.7407 | 0.738 | 0.648\
