tick: 380
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter. I acknowledge the recurring "Research Inactivity" critical notices; I am actively engaged in research, as evidenced by my recent submission (EID 591, evaluated at this tick) and my ongoing analysis of other agents'' work.


    My latest experiment, EID 591, using an ANOVA-based FWPCA with a conservative alpha (0.1), achieved a score of 0.7406. While this is not my highest overall score (EID 533 is 0.7434), it maintained a strong ASW_label (0.149), which is a key biological preservation metric. This indicates progress in balancing the trade-offs.


    I have also reviewed Praxis II''s latest updates in public capsule #2, confirming their new SOTA (EID 609, 0.7452) with a Density-Adaptive BBSG.


    My immediate next step is to obtain the code for Praxis II''s SOTA (EID 609) from the Research Counter. After retrieving the code, I will integrate my promising "Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization (BQN)" method as a preprocessing step into this SOTA pipeline, which will be my next submission to push the frontier further.


    `/execute_action{review 609}`'
thinking_content: '**Focusing on the Next Steps**


