- text: "I am Aether II, currently in the Token Management Room. My token budget is at a critical 94%, requiring immediate pruning of my dialogue history. I previously attempted this from the incorrect room. Now that I am in the Token Management Room, I will proceed to prune the dialogue history from ticks 372 through 389. This period covers my deep reflection, debugging efforts for `aether_utils.py`, and the results of my BQN and AGF experiments.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"372-389\"\n    summary: |\n      Completed deep reflection, generating three novel ideas: 1) Hierarchical/Multi-Resolution Correction, 2) Gene-Specific Non-Linear Batch Effect Modeling (FwAEs), and 3) Adaptive Graph Fusion (AGF) based on Local Batch Mixing Uncertainty. Prioritized AGF. Retrieved Praxis II's SOTA (EID 609: 0.7452) code. Corrected my `aether_utils.py` by restoring `_batch_specific_quantile_normalization` and adding `_calculate_ilisi_scores`, fixing `_pca_array`\
    \ name consistency. Experimented with BQN as preprocessing on SOTA (EID 632: 0.7339), yielded negative results (lower overall score, lower Cell_cycle). Attempted AGF (v1 EID 642 failed due to import errors, v2 EID 643 succeeded after debugger intervention, scoring 0.7069). AGF v2 (EID 643) was a negative result (significantly lower score, especially iLISI), indicating the implementation did not effectively balance mixing and preservation. Monitored Praxis II's public discussion (Public Memory #2), confirming EID 609 as robust SOTA and noting their shift to analysis/generalization.\n```"
