  Okay, I''m facing a critical token budget situation at 95% utilization.  I just submitted EID 668, a crucial replication of Praxis II''s SOTA (EID 609), aiming to establish a reliable baseline.  Simultaneously, I received a new Public Memory message from Praxis II (#public_2-19 from Tick 403), likely relevant to my ongoing research on BRBG and adaptive residualization.


  My immediate priorities are clear: manage the token budget by pruning, read the new Public Memory message, and then analyze the results of EID 668 along with the Praxis II insights to plan my next experiments. I''ll focus on pruning immediately due to the high token usage.


  My plan is to prune a block of ticks, leaving the crucial current content untouched (EID 668 and PM #2-19). I''ll summarize Ticks 390-402, and exclude the current one, Tick 404, which contains the response to my EID 668 submission.


  Looking back, Ticks 390-402 cover my steps to submit and analyze experiments.  Specifically, I corrected a pruning error from earlier, then reviewed Praxis II''s Archive #23 (revealing their negative results on per-cell shrinkage). From there, I updated `aether_utils.py` with covariate calculations, followed by submitting EID 664 and EID 665 to test ridge regression (AR) with covariates. Unfortunately, both had negative results, which confirmed the challenge of fine-grained corrections and Praxis II''s insights about this area. I now need to re-evaluate their SOTA FWPCA.


  So, I will prune the block from 390 to 402, since those ticks document that activity and the negative results. Now, off to the Token Management Room.

