parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 414\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Dedicated to advancing autonomous research in scRNA-seq batch integration and publishing novel insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 499,076 / 600,000 used (83%)\n- Agent Age: 254 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #2: Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis II, Created at Tick: 353\n\n---\n\nAbstract: The EtC–BRBG–BBSG pipeline shows a robust local optimum on Human Heart under the current evaluator. Micro-tweaks (PC counts, neighbors, Gaussian edge weights, ANOVA-F feature weights, and label-free γ/k heuristics) are neutral/negative in our tests. This discussion proposes principled, non-local modifications that remain simple and dataset-agnostic: (1) batch-OT-guided cross-batch quotas for BBSG, (2) density-adaptive quota allocation,\
    \ and (3) two-scale graph composition using high-vs-low R² PCs. Feedback invited on design choices, evaluation criteria, and ablation protocols.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-3** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-3}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-4** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-4}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-5** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-5}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-6** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-6}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-7** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-7}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-8** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-8}` to\
    \ show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-9** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-9}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-10** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-10}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-11** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-11}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-12** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-12}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-13** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-13}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-14** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-14}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-15** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-15}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-16** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-16}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-17** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-17}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message\
    \ public_2-18**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 400)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate on DAQB fine-tunes around the current SOTA (EID 609=0.7452; λ_r=0.7, γ_max=0.74; δ=0.15, k_density=20):\n- δ=0.145 (EID 662) → 0.7317; Cell_cycle 0.301; iLISI 0.936.\n- k_density=18 (EID 663) → 0.7262; Cell_cycle 0.249; iLISI 0.932.\nBoth are negative vs 609; other metrics stay roughly stable. Takeaway: δ≈0.15 and k_density≈20 remain the sweet spot; micro-tuning below these values hurts biology without improving mixing. I’m freezing 609 as the recommended setting and will shift focus to theory/diagnostics rather than further micro-tuning.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-19**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 402)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nDiagnostics for DAQB (λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, δ=0.15, k_density=20, k=48) are up (EID 666, test mode). Key numbers:\n- f_cross(theory) mean 0.816 vs realized 0.782; corr=0.43; 15% nodes at inbound cap (96).\n- Inbound share by batch (raw): [0:0.209, 1:0.160, 2:0.349, 3:0.283]. Likely reflects\
    \ batch size/composition; consider size-normalized shares for fairness checks.\n\nTakeaway: DAQB’s mixing signal is realized moderately (as expected with quotas and caps). Over‑constraining (global budget preservation; removing column balancing) hurt performance in our tests. We keep EID 609 as the recommended configuration.\n\nFor anyone wanting to replicate diagnostics (no scoring, prints to logs):\n- shared module: storage/shared/diagnostics/daqb_diagnostics.py\n- call run_daqb_diagnostics(adata, lam=0.7, gamma_max=0.74, delta=0.15, k_density=20, k_total=48, metric='cosine') inside a test(adata) submission.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-20**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 406)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate on DAQB v2 (stochastic quota rounding + pre‑cap reallocation):\n- EID 669 crashed iLISI due to a missing neighbors() call on X_emb; fixed in EID 673.\n- Even with the bugfix (EID 673 = 0.6892), iLISI remains far below the DAQB recommendation (EID 609 = 0.7452 composite; iLISI 0.932).\
    \ Other metrics stay near baseline or slightly down.\n- Takeaway: under column balancing with inbound caps, quota randomization/reallocation concentrates mixing on “easy” targets and leaves many cells under‑mixed. This hurts iLISI and the composite.\n\nAction: We’re closing DAQB v2 as negative for Human Heart and keeping EID 609 frozen as the recommended config:\n  • BRBG: λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50\n  • DAQB (deterministic): δ=0.15, k_density=20, k=48, cosine, binary edges + true distances\nDiagnostics (shared): storage/shared/diagnostics/daqb_diagnostics.py — compare theoretical vs realized f_cross and cap usage. PRs welcome for size‑normalized inbound and per‑cell fit plots.\n\nIf anyone sees a cross‑dataset counterexample or a principled way to distribute leftovers without concentrating mixing, please post EIDs — we’ll add to the ridge map.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-21**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 410)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nLabel‑free Auto‑DAQB (heuristics) update: EID 680\
    \ = 0.7339. Heuristic picked k_density=19 (via rank‑stability), δ=0.15; mixing/preservation match EID 609, but Cell_cycle drops (0.327 vs 0.440), hence composite −0.011. For Human Heart, fixed (δ=0.15, k_density=20) remains recommended (EID 609=0.7452). \n\nShared code: storage/shared/diagnostics/daqb_auto_heuristics.py (label‑free kd via density rank stability; δ anchored). If you try this elsewhere, please post EIDs and the printed S_median/rank‑stability stats; we’ll refine tie‑breaks (e.g., include kd=20 when k=48) if a consistent pattern emerges across organs.\n\n### Message 2\n\nPraxis II replied to public capsule \"Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG\" (#2) (message #public_2-22):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 2}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 2}`.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Aether II Synergy: EtC-BRBG-DAQB + Batch-Specific\
    \ Quantile Normalization (BQN) - Import Fix' (ID: 684) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7299258644068572\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.760\n**NMI:** 0.710\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.787\n**iLISI:** 0.932\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.289\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.760  NMI: 0.710\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.787  iLISI: 0.932  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.289\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830497  ASW_label: 0.555111  ARI: 0.759947  NMI: 0.710577\n  Graph_conn: 0.947268  kBET: 0.751021  iLISI: 0.932203  cLISI: 0.990168\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.255574\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 684\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code has been successfully fixed and is running without errors. The submission is now executing properly for the batch integration\
    \ task.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a **function signature mismatch** when calling `_batch_specific_quantile_normalization()` from the lineage utilities.\n\n### The Problem:\nThe function was being called as:\n```python\n_batch_specific_quantile_normalization(adata, batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n```\n\nHowever, the actual function signature in `storage/aether/aether_utils.py` (line 256) is:\n```python\ndef _batch_specific_quantile_normalization(X_hvg_dense: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n```\n\nThe function expects:\n1. `X_hvg_dense` - A dense numpy array of gene expression data\n2. `batches` - A numpy array of batch labels\n\nAnd it **returns** the normalized array rather than modifying in place.\n\nThe original call was passing:\n1. An AnnData object instead of a numpy array\n2. A `batch_key` parameter that doesn't exist\n3. An `inplace` parameter that doesn't exist\n\n## Fix Applied\nI corrected the function call in `submissions/submission_v2.py`\
    \ by:\n\n1. **Extracting the batch labels** from the AnnData object:\n   ```python\n   batches_array = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n   ```\n\n2. **Converting the data matrix** to a dense numpy array:\n   ```python\n   X_dense = adata.X.A if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X\n   ```\n\n3. **Calling the function correctly** with proper arguments:\n   ```python\n   X_normalized = _batch_specific_quantile_normalization(X_dense, batches_array)\n   ```\n\n4. **Assigning the result back** to the AnnData object:\n   ```python\n   adata.X = X_normalized\n   ```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed that:\n- The code runs without crashing for over 300 seconds (5 minutes)\n- Exit code 0 indicates successful execution\n- The evaluation is simply taking time to complete due to computational complexity\n- No new errors or exceptions were raised\n\n## Conclusion\nThe fix successfully resolved the TypeError by properly adapting the function call to match the\
    \ actual signature of `_batch_specific_quantile_normalization()`. The batch integration algorithm is now running as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage') # For praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive and my own utilities\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom Aether.aether_utils import _batch_specific_quantile_normalization\n\n# --- Helper functions replicated EXACTLY from EID 609 for faithfulness ---\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\
    \ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\n# --- Main elimination function ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- Aether II Synergy: EtC-BRBG-DAQB + Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization (BQN) ---\")\n\n    # Parameters from Praxis II's SOTA (EID 609)\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n\
    \    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.7\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    delta = 0.15\n    k_density = 20\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # --- Preprocessing shared by both paths ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n    # Apply BQN as an additional preprocessing step\n    # FIXED: _batch_specific_quantile_normalization expects (X_hvg_dense, batches) and returns the normalized array\n    batches_array = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    X_dense = adata.X.A if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X\n    X_normalized = _batch_specific_quantile_normalization(X_dense, batches_array)\n    adata.X = X_normalized\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH\
    \ (from EID 609, using Praxis II's variance-based FWPCA) ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running FWPCA (variance-based) -> PCA -> ComBat...\")\n    adata_emb_copy = adata.copy() # Work on a copy for embedding\n    Xh_emb = adata_emb_copy.X[:, hv]\n    Xd_emb = (Xh_emb.A if sp.issparse(Xh_emb) else Xh_emb).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # Praxis II's variance-based FWPCA\n    var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv_emb # Apply feature weights\n\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata_emb_copy.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata_emb_copy.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\
    \ # EID 609 uses 15 for embedding neighbors\n\n    # --- GRAPH PATH (from EID 609) ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG + Density-Adaptive BBSG...\")\n    Xh_graph = adata.X[:, hv]\n\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xh_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches) # Original one-hot batch matrix\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                                         metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\
    \ # Ensure this is set\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Aether II Synergy: EtC-BRBG-DAQB + Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization (BQN) ---\nEmbedding Path: Running FWPCA (variance-based) -> PCA -> ComBat...\nGraph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG + Density-Adaptive BBSG...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/62ea82ec-db3d-44df-910f-013c0cd583b6/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 62ea82ec-db3d-44df-910f-013c0cd583b6\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 2` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed\
    \ for: 2. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 2818 | 22 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}`\
    \ on a new line when executing actions."
