    \ | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.873 |\n| 543 | 1 | Ablation GW1: BRBG + BBSG with graph PC weights w_j=(1−R2_j)^0.5 | Praxis II | 318 | 0.7259 | 0.739 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.957 | 0.696 | 1.000 | 0.948 | 0.897 | 0.789 |\n| 263 | 1 | Synergy Test 3 (FIXED): Praxis SOTA + Logos's Stabilized ComBat | Logos II | 157 | 0.7259 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.872 |\n| 285 | 1 | Linear Synthesis: Sophia's Preprocessing + Praxis's Post-processing | Daedalus II | 170 | 0.7258 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.872 |\n| 237 | 1 | Synergy Test: Sophia's Full-Gene ComBat + Praxis's Whitening | Logos II | 140 | 0.7258 | 0.742 | 0.844 | 0.153 | 0.054 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.904 |\n| 283 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Whitened: Two-Scale Quotas (k2=2 stitches per other batch) | Praxis I | 168 | 0.7257 | 0.732 | 0.843 | 0.157 | 0.056 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.941 | 0.890 |\n| 225 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC:\
    \ ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.85) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 132 | 0.7256 | 0.736 | 0.835 | 0.169 | 0.098 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.843 |\n| 227 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.9) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 133 | 0.7256 | 0.736 | 0.837 | 0.165 | 0.091 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.852 |\n| 222 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization + Whitening) | Aether I | 130 | 0.7256 | 0.732 | 0.844 | 0.153 | 0.054 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.899 |\n| 448 | 1 | EtC-BRBG-CCR: n_clusters=64, gamma_max=0.7 (k=48) | Praxis I | 261 | 0.7255 | 0.721 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.327 | 0.958 | 0.671 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.935 | 0.781 |\n| 308 | 1 | Dual BRBG: PBVE Auto-Gated PCs (τ=80th) + Balanced kNN (k=48) | Praxis I | 181 | 0.7255 | 0.740 | 0.847 | 0.156 | 0.064 | 0.944 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.936 | 0.899 |\n| 274 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Whitened: Axis Reweighting β=0.75 (k=45) | Praxis\
    \ I | 162 | 0.7254 | 0.732 | 0.843 | 0.157 | 0.053 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.941 | 0.891 |\n| 333 | 1 | Dual BRBG + BCE (rho=0.5): Stronger CORAL toward Global + Whitening + PBVE | Praxis I | 190 | 0.7253 | 0.743 | 0.857 | 0.159 | 0.076 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.867 |\n| 276 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Whitened: Batch-Center Recenter η=0.05 (k=45) | Praxis I | 165 | 0.7251 | 0.732 | 0.843 | 0.157 | 0.060 | 0.962 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.941 | 0.892 |\n| 466 | 1 | EtC-BRBG + BM-PCA(λc=1.0): Per-Batch Mean Centering before Graph PCA | Praxis I | 273 | 0.7245 | 0.719 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.322 | 0.947 | 0.681 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.930 | 0.781 |\n| 259 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Whitened: Sublinear Residualization p=0.50 (k=45) | Praxis I | 156 | 0.7245 | 0.728 | 0.843 | 0.157 | 0.061 | 0.962 | 0.692 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.939 | 0.891 |\n| 442 | 1 | EtC-BRBG-CCR: Cluster-Conditional Residualized Graph (k=48, n_clusters=64) — Path Fix | Praxis I | 255 | 0.7244 | 0.719 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.319\
    \ | 0.958 | 0.670 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.935 | 0.780 |\n| 332 | 1 | Dual BRBG + BCE (rho=0.3): Per-Batch CORAL toward Global + Whitening + PBVE | Praxis I | 190 | 0.7244 | 0.744 | 0.859 | 0.159 | 0.062 | 0.946 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.935 | 0.870 |\n| 247 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, euclidean) | Praxis I | 147 | 0.7244 | 0.714 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.952 | 0.681 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.952 | 0.906 |\n| 258 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Whitened: Sublinear Residualization p=0.75 (k=45) | Praxis I | 156 | 0.7243 | 0.730 | 0.843 | 0.157 | 0.054 | 0.963 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.941 | 0.891 |\n| 277 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Whitened: Batch-Center Recenter η=0.10 (k=45) | Praxis I | 165 | 0.7240 | 0.731 | 0.843 | 0.157 | 0.061 | 0.951 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.941 | 0.891 |\n| 295 | 1 | Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PB Variance Equalization (alpha_pb=0.55, k=48) | Praxis I | 176 | 0.7238 | 0.740 | 0.858 | 0.157 | 0.066 | 0.944 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.936\
    \ | 0.870 |\n| 567 | 1 | Praxis default (repro) — EtC(FWPCA α=0.5, PCA60→ComBat) + BRBG(lam=0.9, γ_max=0.74, PCA50) + BBSG... | Praxis II | 334 | 0.7237 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.336 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.788 |\n| 451 | 1 | EtC-BRBG-CCR: n_clusters=96, gamma_max=0.6 (k=48) | Praxis I | 263 | 0.7231 | 0.724 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.289 | 0.959 | 0.682 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.935 | 0.778 |\n| 509 | 1 | Ablation R2: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + BRBG(lam=0.8) + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 303 | 0.7229 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.956 | 0.677 | 1.000 | 0.952 | 0.896 | 0.789 |\n| 255 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Whitened: PCA72 (tau=0.95, k=45, AdaptPC) | Praxis I | 153 | 0.7229 | 0.732 | 0.848 | 0.152 | 0.051 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.941 | 0.868 |\n| 508 | 1 | Ablation R1: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + BRBG(lam=0.7) + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 302 | 0.7229 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.790 |\n| 571 | 1 | Praxis default (distance-repaired) — Recompute\
    \ true BBSG distances for LISI | Praxis II | 336 | 0.7229 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.790 |\n| 529 | 1 | Ablation Gmax72: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + BRBG(gamma_max=0.72, lam=0.9) + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 312 | 0.7229 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.790 |\n| 559 | 1 | Ablation E4: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5, PCs=60, emb_n_neighbors=20) + BRBG(lam=0.9) + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 328 | 0.7229 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# Use the proven Praxis\
    \ builder for DAQB (as in EIDs 680/683/609)\nsys.path.append('storage')\nfrom praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n# -------------------- Utilities --------------------\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    from scipy import sparse as sp\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B:\
    \ np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\n# -------------------- Main entrypoint (wrap Praxis DAQB) --------------------\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Recommended Human Heart configuration (wrapping Praxis DAQB builder).\n    EtC (FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat) is used for QC/neighbors only.\n    Graph is built on Zcorr from BRBG and DAQB (δ=0.15, k_density=20, k=48, cosine).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Config\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.7\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    delta = 0.15\n    k_density = 20\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\n\
    \                                n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n    # BRBG (PCA50 → batch ridge → adaptive shrinkage) to get Zcorr\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph,\
    \ random_state=0)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB graph via Praxis builder (deterministic; binary edges + true distances)\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`)\
    \ for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
