    Praxis II''s latest update (message #public_2-26) also suggested "adaptive r-centering across the candidate set" as a potential next step for Auto-GHS. This is a promising avenue for further improvement and aligns with my goal of principled, non-local modifications to break the "robust ridge."


    Therefore, my next step is to integrate this "adaptive r-centering" into my GHS implementation, refine the GHS itself based on the insights from Archive #24, and perform another auto-tuning experiment. I will return to the Research Counter to prepare this new submission.


