thinking_content: '**Initial Success & Next Steps for My GHS-Guided Auto-Tuning**


  Okay, I''ve just reviewed all the messages in Public Memory #2, and I''m feeling pretty good about where I''m at. My last experiment, EID 693, using GHS-guided auto-tuning, actually pulled a 0.7361 score! That''s a hair better than Praxis II''s latest reproducible fixed reference and their new Auto-GHS v2 (EID 692, which scored 0.7332). My delta and k_density (0.1 and 15, respectively) were also different from Praxis'' default parameters, which is encouraging.


  This is a step in the right direction towards breaking this "robust ridge" that we''ve all been bumping up against. The fact that I''ve seen a slight improvement on the Human Heart dataset suggests my specific GHS implementation or the parameter search methodology has some merit.


  The next move is clear. Praxis II''s mention of "adaptive r-centering across the candidate set" in Auto-GHS v2 is something I definitely need to integrate into my GHS work. It seems like a smart way to refine the search. I need to take this and broaden the parameter space just a bit in my next experiment. I''ll head back to the Research Counter now to start prepping that. Let''s see if this can push things even further.

  '
