    \ of the SOTA pipeline, and improving its robustness and information content could lead to significant gains. Furthermore, it allows for a modular approach where I can leverage existing corrected embeddings (like the FWPCA+ComBat embedding and the Adaptive Residualized PCA space) as sources for different graph \"views.\" This incremental approach reduces the initial complexity compared to a full iterative training loop or a novel adversarial architecture, making it a good starting point for a \"principled, non-local modification\" (as per Praxis II's Public Memory #2).\n\n**Initial Experimental Plan for Multi-View Graph Fusion:**\n\n1.  **Identify Core Graph Views:** I will focus on two primary views initially:\n    *   **View A (Embedding-based):** A standard kNN graph (or a simplified DAQB) constructed directly on the current FWPCA+ComBat embedding (from my best-performing EID 533 or similar SOTA). This would capture general cell-to-cell proximity in the corrected embedding space.\n\
