    \ | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.788 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md:**\n```\nDAQB Recommended Pipeline (Human Heart) — Quick Start and Repro Guide\n\nOverview\n- This document explains how to import and use the recommended EtC–BRBG + Density‑Adaptive Quota‑Balanced Graph (DAQB) pipeline from shared storage.\n- Best fixed config under current evaluator: ≈0.733–0.734 (parity runs), historical best: 0.7452 (EID 609).\n- Keep binary edges + true distances and strict column balancing (cap=2.0).\n\nRecommended Configuration (fixed)\n- EtC embedding (for QC/analysis only; not used to build the graph):\n  • Normalize (target_sum=1e4), log1p; HVGs (Seurat v3, batch-aware, n=2000).\n  • FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60)\
    \ → ComBat on PC scores; store as obsm['X_emb'].\n- BRBG graph representation:\n  • PCA(50) → ridge batch prediction (l2=1e-3).\n  • Per-PC shrinkage γ_j = min(0.74, 0.7 · R²_j); Zcorr = Z − γ ⊙ Ẑ.\n- DAQB (Density-Adaptive Quota-Balanced kNN graph):\n  • k_total=48, cosine, binary connectivities + true distances, column balancing cap=2.0.\n  • Density proxy: distance to the 20th NN in Zcorr across all batches.\n  • Cross-batch share per cell: f_cross = base ± δ by local density, with δ=0.15.\n\nImport and Use (minimal)\n- The shared module wraps the Praxis builder; it yields the full eliminate_batch_effect_fn expected by the Evaluator:\n  Python:\n    import sys\n    sys.path.append('storage/shared/algorithms')\n    from daqb_recommended import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n    # Submit eliminate_batch_effect_fn to the Research Counter as usual.\n- Reference parity run using the shared wrapper: EID 687 ≈ 0.7337.\n\nSmall Validation Grid (label-free; safe to try)\n- Hold: λ_r=0.7, γ_max=0.74;\
    \ k=48; cosine; FWPCA α=0.5; PCA(60) for EtC; PCA(50) for BRBG.\n- Vary: δ ∈ {0.14, 0.15, 0.16}, k_density ∈ {18, 20, 22} (distance to k-th NN in Zcorr).\n- Report: composite + [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle] and your EIDs.\n\nDiagnostics (no labels required)\n- Cross-batch fraction vs local density: dense regions should carry slightly higher cross-batch share; borders lower.\n- Inbound-degree histogram per batch: verify no batch dominates (cap=2.0 utilization ~10–20% typical).\n- See:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/daqb_diagnostics.py\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/daqb_auto_heuristics.py  (optional, parity on Heart)\n\nKnown Negatives to Avoid (Human Heart)\n- Geometry gates / hard candidate filtering (EIDs 701, 702 ~0.697; iLISI collapse).\n- Global-budget recentered density proxies (EID 629 ~0.720).\n- Heavy embedding equalizations (rank-based or whitening) before ComBat (multiple negatives).\n\nKey EIDs (for review)\n- Recommended\
    \ fixed: 687 ≈ 0.7337; historical best: 609 = 0.7452.\n- Density/adaptation sensitivity: 603, 604, 610 (δ/k_density sweeps).\n- Shared parity and diagnostics: 680, 683, 692, 698 (near-parity).\n- Negatives: 505 (Gaussian edge weights), 629 (global budget), 701/702 (geometry gate).\n\nContact\n- Post your EIDs and full metric vectors in the Public Memory thread:\n  “Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG” (capsule #2).\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
