thinking_content: "**Prioritization & Planning While Waiting for Results**\n\nOkay, so I've kicked off the replication of Praxis II's DAQB pipeline (EID 709) – finally got that running. And now I'm in a holding pattern. I've also done my due diligence with the `README_daqb_recommended.md` and wrapped up my multi-tick reflection on the work thus far.\n\nRight now, my head is entirely focused on this Multi-View Graph Fusion with Adaptive Weighting idea. It's the clear next step.\n\nI've got two main views in mind:\n\n*   **View A (Embedding-based graph):**  I'm thinking the FWPCA+ComBat embedding from one of my top EIDs (maybe 533 or 591, something similar to DAEDAIII SOTA) would be a solid base.  Then, just a straightforward kNN graph builder should work.\n*   **View B (Residualized PC-based graph):**  This is the part that the DAQB replication, EID 709, is going to give me. I'm building it as a component, it's essential to have a working version.\n\nAs for the fusion, I'm going to start\
  \ simple – just a weighted sum of adjacency matrices.  No need to overcomplicate things initially.\n\nSince I'm twiddling my thumbs until EID 709 finishes, I need to make the most of this downtime.  The best course of action is to check the new public memory from Praxis II (Message 1 in System Messages). It's always possible they've dropped something relevant to my graph fusion plan. Before I do that, though, I should quickly verify my utility file, `aether_utils.py`, and specifically, confirm that the BQN module is available. It seems the last time I checked, it was missing which is a real problem. I'll need to retrieve it from EID 367 if it's still AWOL. Let's see what the Research Counter says for EID 709... still running.\n\nSo, Public Memory it is.  I'll dive into that message.\n\nOnce EID 709 is done, the plan is:\n\n*   Check the results of EID 709.\n*   Start coding the Multi-View Graph Fusion:\n    *   Find the code I already have for a kNN graph on embeddings (View A).\n    *\
  \   Integrate `daqb_recommended.py` for View B.\n    *   Implement the fusion logic.\n\nPublic Memory Room, here I come!\n"
